# IntraCore: параметры HAL блока из базы STM32CubeMX (db/mcu/IP/*_Modes.xml).
# Порождено tools/hal_import — руками не править. Формат: src/Docs/Description/HalCatalogFormat.md
[Ip]
Name=NetXDuo
Version=v1.0.0_WBA_Cube

[Parameters]
# имя|подпись|группа|единица|мин|макс|описание
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_PREEMPTION_THRESHOLD|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_PREEMPTION_THRESHOLD|SNTP||0|255|This option sets the sets the level of priority at which the Client thread allows preemption. The default NetX Duo SNTP Client value is set to NX_SNTP_CLIENT_ THREAD_PRIORITY.
NX_DHCP_SLOW_PERIODIC_TIME_INTERVAL|NX_DHCP_SLOW_PERIODIC_TIME_INTERVAL|DHCP||0|2147483647|This is timeout period in timer ticks for the DHCP Server slow timer to check on IP address lease time remaining and handle lease that have timed out.
NX_DHCP_CLIENT_HOSTNAME_MAX|NX_DHCP_CLIENT_HOSTNAME_MAX|DHCP||1|255|This is size of the buffer for holding the Client host name in the current DHCP Server Client session. The default value is 32.
NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_ERROR_MESSAGE|NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_ERROR_MESSAGE|ICMP||||Defined, disables NetX Duo from sending an ICMPv6 error message in response to a problem packet (e.g., improperly formatted header or packet header type is deprecated) received from another host.
NX_DHCPV6_MAX_LEASES|NX_DHCPV6_MAX_LEASES|DHCP||1|65535|Defines the size of the Server’s IP lease table (e.g. the max number of IPv6 address available to lease that can be stored). By default, this value is 100.
NX_DISABLE_UDP_TX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_UDP_TX_CHECKSUM|UDP||||Defined, disables the UDP checksum computation on outgoing UDP packets. This is useful if the network interface driver is able to compute UDP header checksum and insert the value in the IP head before transmitting the data, and the application does not enable IPsec or IP fragmentation logic.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MAX_TIME_ADJUSTMENT|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MAX_TIME_ADJUSTMENT|SNTP||0|2147483647|The maximum time adjustment in milliseconds the Client will make to its local clock time. For time adjustments above this amount, the local clock adjustment is limited to the maximum time adjustment. The NetX Duo SNTP Client default is 180000 (3 minutes).
NX_DHCP_MIN_RENEW_TIMEOUT|NX_DHCP_MIN_RENEW_TIMEOUT|DHCP||0|2147483647|Specifies minimum wait option for receiving a DHCP Server message and sending a renewal request after the DHCP Client is bound to an IP address. The default value is 60 seconds. However, the DHCP Client uses the Renew and Rebind expiration times from the DHCP server message before defaulting to the minimum renew timeout.
NX_DHCP_CLIENT_USER_CREATE_PACKET_POOL|NX_DHCP_CLIENT_USER_CREATE_PACKET_POOL|DHCP||||If set, the DHCP Client will not create its own packet pool. The host application must use the nx_dhcp_packet_pool_set service to set the DHCP Client packet pool. The default value is disabled.
NX_DHCPV6_SESSION_TIMEOUT|NX_DHCPV6_SESSION_TIMEOUT|DHCP||0|65535|Define the session time out in seconds. This is the timer for how long the server has not received a client response. The default value is set to 20.
NX_DHCPV6_FRAGMENT_OPTION|NX_DHCPV6_FRAGMENT_OPTION|DHCP||||This defines the Server socket fragmentation option. The default value is NX_DONT_FRAGMENT.
NX_DHCP_CLIENT_SEND_MAX_DHCP_MESSAGE_OPTION|NX_DHCP_CLIENT_SEND_MAX_DHCP_MESSAGE_OPTION|DHCP||||Defined, this enables the DHCP Client to send maximum DHCP message size option. By default, this option is disabled.
NX_WEB_HTTP_MAX_HEADER_FIELD|NX_WEB_HTTP_MAX_HEADER_FIELD|WEB Server||0|65535|Specifies the maximum size of the HTTP header field. The default value is 256.
NX_TCP_ACK_TIMER_RATE|NX_TCP_ACK_TIMER_RATE|TCP||0|65535|Specifies how the number of system ticks (NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE) is divided to calculate the timer rate for the TCP delayed ACK processing. The default value is 5, which represents 200ms, and is defined in nx_tcp.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_DISABLE_TCP_RX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_TCP_RX_CHECKSUM|TCP||||Defined, disables checksum logic on received TCP packets. This is only useful in situations in which the link-layer has reliable checksum or CRC processing, or the interface driver is able to verify the TCP checksum in hardware, and the application does not use IPsec.
NX_ICMPV6_MAX_RTR_SOLICITATIONS|NX_ICMPV6_MAX_RTR_SOLICITATIONS|ICMP||0|65535|Define the max number of router solicitations a host sends until a router response is received. If no response is received, the host concludes no router is present. The default value is 3.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_THREAD_STACK_SIZE|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_THREAD_STACK_SIZE|SNTP||1|2147483647|This option sets the size of the Client thread stack. The default NetX Duo SNTP Client size is 2048.
NX_DNS_IP_GATEWAY_AND_DNS_SERVER|NX_DNS_IP_GATEWAY_AND_DNS_SERVER|DNS||||If defined and the Client IPv4 gateway address is non zero, the DNS Client sets the IPv4 gateway as the Client’s primary DNS server. The default value is disabled.
NX_DHCP_THREAD_STACK_SIZE|NX_DHCP_THREAD_STACK_SIZE|DHCP||1|65535|Size of the DHCP thread stack. By default, the size is 4096 bytes.
NX_CRYPTO_HMAC_MAX_PAD_SIZE|NX_CRYPTO_HMAC_MAX_PAD_SIZE|CRYPTO HMAC||1|65535|This option defines the hmac max pad size.
NX_SECURE_DISABLE_X509|NX_SECURE_DISABLE_X509|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option disables X509 feature.
NX_SECURE_X509_CRL_VERIFY_EXTENSION|NX_SECURE_X509_CRL_VERIFY_EXTENSION|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables X509 crl verify extension.
NX_SNTP_SERVER_UDP_PORT|NX_SNTP_SERVER_UDP_PORT|SNTP||0|65535|This is port which the Client sends SNTP messages to the SNTP Server on. The default NetX SNTP Server port is 123.
NX_TCP_KEEPALIVE_RETRY|NX_TCP_KEEPALIVE_RETRY|TCP||0|65535|Specifies the number of seconds between retries of the keepalive timer assuming the other side of the connection is not responding. The default value is 75, which represents 75 seconds between retries, and is defined in nx_tcp.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_ENABLE_PACKET_DEBUG_INFO|NX_ENABLE_PACKET_DEBUG_INFO|Core||||Defined, logs packet debug information.
NX_PPP_PASSWORD_SIZE|NX_PPP_PASSWORD_SIZE|PPP||0|65535|Specifies the size of “password” strings used in authentication. The default value is set to 32bytes, but can be redefined prior to inclusion of nx_ppp.h.
NX_DHCP_PACKET_PAYLOAD|NX_DHCP_PACKET_PAYLOAD|DHCP||0|65535|Specifies the size in bytes of the DHCP Client packet payload. The default value is NX_DHCP_MINIMUM_IP_DATAGRAM + physical header size. The physical header size in a wireline network is usually the Ethernet frame size.
NX_DHCP_FAST_PERIODIC_TIME_INTERVAL|NX_DHCP_FAST_PERIODIC_TIME_INTERVAL|DHCP||0|2147483647|This is timeout period in timer ticks for the DHCP Server fast timer to check on session time remaining and handle sessions that have timed out.
NX_DHCPV6_THREAD_PRIORITY|NX_DHCPV6_THREAD_PRIORITY|DHCP||0|255|Priority of the Client thread. By default, this value specifies that the Client thread runs at priority 2.
NX_DISABLE_IGMPV2|NX_DISABLE_IGMPV2|IGMP||||Defined, disables IGMPv2 support, and NetX Duo supports IGMPv1 only. By default this option is not set and is defined in nx_api.h.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_RETRY_SHIFT|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_RETRY_SHIFT|WEB Server||0|2147483647|This value is used to set the next retransmission timeout. The current timeout is multiplied by the number of retransmissions thus far, shifted by the value of the socket timeout shift.
NX_DNS_PACKET_PAYLOAD_UNALIGNED|NX_DNS_PACKET_PAYLOAD_UNALIGNED|DNS||0|2147483647|If not defined, the size of the Client packet payload which includes the Ethernet, IP (or IPv6), and UDP headers plus the maximum DNS message size specified by NX_DNS_MESSAGE_MAX. Regardless if defined, the packet payload is the 4-byte aligned and stored in NX_DNS_PACKET_PAYLOAD. The default value is (NX_UDP_PACKET + NX_DNS_MESSAGE_MAX).
NX_WEB_HTTP_MAX_NAME|NX_WEB_HTTP_MAX_NAME|WEB Server||0|65535|Specifies the number of bytes allowed in a client supplied username. The default value is set to 20.
NX_TCP_MAXIMUM_SEGMENT_LIFETIME|NX_TCP_MAXIMUM_SEGMENT_LIFETIME|TCP||0|65535|Number of seconds for maximum segment lifetime, the default is 2 minutes (120s)
NX_TCP_ACK_EVERY_N_PACKETS|NX_TCP_ACK_EVERY_N_PACKETS|TCP||0|65535|Specifies the number of TCP packets to receive before sending an ACK. Note if NX_TCP_IMMEDIATE_ACK is enabled but NX_TCP_ACK_EVERY_N_PACKETS is not, this value is automatically set to 1 for backward compatibility.
NX_DHCP_CLIENT_RECORD_TABLE_SIZE|NX_DHCP_CLIENT_RECORD_TABLE_SIZE|DHCP||1|65535|This is size of the DHCP Server array for holding Client records. The default value is 50.
NX_AUTO_IP_PROBE_NUM|NX_AUTO_IP_PROBE_NUM|AUTO_IP||0|65535|The number of ARP probes to send. By default, this value is defined as 3.
NX_DISABLE_TCP_TX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_TCP_TX_CHECKSUM|TCP||||Defined, disables checksum logic for sending TCP packets. This is only useful in situations in which the receiving network node has received TCP checksum logic disabled or the underlying network driver is capable of generating the TCP checksum, and the application does not use IPsec.
NX_DHCP_IP_ADDRESS_MAX_LIST_SIZE|NX_DHCP_IP_ADDRESS_MAX_LIST_SIZE|DHCP||1|65535|This is size of the DHCP Server array for holding available IP addresses for assigning to the Client. The default value is 20.
NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_DUID_VENDOR_PRIVATE_ID|NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_DUID_VENDOR_PRIVATE_ID|DHCP||0x00000000|0xFFFFFFFF|Sets the enterprise type of the DUID to private vendor type.
NX_DHCP_OPTIONS_BUFFER_SIZE|NX_DHCP_OPTIONS_BUFFER_SIZE|DHCP||1|65535|Size of DHCP options buffer. By default, this value is 312 bytes.
NX_DISABLE_ARP_INFO|NX_DISABLE_ARP_INFO|ARP/RARP||||Defined, disables ARP information gathering.
NX_TCP_FAST_TIMER_RATE|NX_TCP_FAST_TIMER_RATE|TCP||0|65535|Specifies how the number of NetX Duo internal ticks (NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE) is divided to calculate the fast TCP timer rate. The fast TCP timer is used to drive the various TCP timers, including the delayed ACK timer. The default value is 10, which represents 100ms assuming the ThreadX timer is running at 10ms. This value is defined in nx_tcp.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_SECURE_TLS_PREMASTER_SIZE|NX_SECURE_TLS_PREMASTER_SIZE|TLS CORE||1|65535|This option defines the sie of pre-master secret. The pre-master secret should be at least 66 bytes for ECDH/ECDHE with secp521r1 (The default value is 68). The pre-master secret is 48 bytes, except for PSK ciphersuites for which it may be more.
NX_PPP_DEBUG_LOG_SIZE|NX_PPP_DEBUG_LOG_SIZE|PPP||1|2147483647|Size of debug log (number of entries in the debug log). On reaching the last entry, the debug capture wraps to the first entry and overwrites any data previously captured. The default value is 50.
NX_SECURE_AEAD_CIPHER_CHECK|NX_SECURE_AEAD_CIPHER_CHECK|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables AEAD ciphersuites other than AES-CCM or AES-GCM working.
NX_ENABLE_TCP_MSS_CHECK|NX_ENABLE_TCP_MSS_CHECK|TCP||||Defined, enables the verification of minimum peer MSS before accepting a TCP connection. To use this feature, the symbol NX_ENABLE_TCP_MSS_MINIMUM must be defined. By default, this option is not enabled.
NX_PACKET_HEADER_PAD|NX_PACKET_HEADER_PAD|TCP||||Defined, NX_PACKET structure is padded for alignment purpose. The default is no padding.
NX_PACKET_HEADER_PAD_SIZE|NX_PACKET_HEADER_PAD_SIZE|TCP||0|65535|Symbol that defines the padding size.
NX_CRYPTO_HUGE_NUMBER_BITS|NX_CRYPTO_HUGE_NUMBER_BITS|CRYPTO CORE||0|65535|This option defines the huge number bits.
NX_DHCPV6_MAX_IA_ADDRESS|NX_DHCPV6_MAX_IA_ADDRESS|DHCP||1|65535|The maximum number of IA addresses that can be added to the Client record. The default value is 1.
NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_TC_DELAY_RANGE|NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_TC_DELAY_RANGE|mDNS||0|2147483647|The delay range, in ticks, in responding to a query with TC bit. The default value is 10 ticks for 100ms.
NX_SECURE_X509_CERTIFICATE_INITIALIZE_EXTENSION|NX_SECURE_X509_CERTIFICATE_INITIALIZE_EXTENSION|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables X509 certificate initialize extension.
NX_PPP_DISABLE_PAP|NX_PPP_DISABLE_PAP|PPP||||If defined, internal PPP PAP logic is removed.
NX_SECURE_TLS_CLIENT_DISABLED|NX_SECURE_TLS_CLIENT_DISABLED|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option removes all TLS/DTLS stack code related to Client mode, reducing code and data usage.
NX_SECURE_X509_CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_EXTENSION|NX_SECURE_X509_CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_EXTENSION|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables certificate verify extension.
NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_THREAD_STACK_SIZE|NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_THREAD_STACK_SIZE|DHCP||0|65535|This defines the size of the DHCPv6 thread stack. By default, the size is 4096 bytes which is more than enough for most NetX Duo applications.
NX_TCP_TRANSMIT_TIMER_RATE|NX_TCP_TRANSMIT_TIMER_RATE|TCP||0|65535|Specifies how the number of system ticks (NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE) is divided to calculate the timer rate for the TCP transmit retry processing. The default value is 1, which represents 1 second, and is defined in nx_tcp.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_ENABLE_TCP_WINDOW_SCALING|NX_ENABLE_TCP_WINDOW_SCALING|TCP||||Enables the window scaling option for TCP applications. If defined, window scaling option is negotiated during TCP connection phase, and the application is able to specify a window size larger than 64K. The default setting is not enabled (not defined).
NX_SECURE_DISABLE_ERROR_CHECKING|NX_SECURE_DISABLE_ERROR_CHECKING|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option removes the basic NetX Secure error checking. It is typically used after the application has been debugged.
NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_NOT_ON_LINK|NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_NOT_ON_LINK|DHCP||||This defines the status option message for : NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_NOT_ON_LINK. The default value is "IA OPTION NOT GRANTED-CLIENT NOT ON LINK".
NX_AUTO_IP_ANNOUNCE_NUM|NX_AUTO_IP_ANNOUNCE_NUM|AUTO_IP||0|65535|The number of ARP announces to send. By default, this value is defined as 2.
NX_PPP_MAX_LCP_PROTOCOL_RETRIES|NX_PPP_MAX_LCP_PROTOCOL_RETRIES|PPP||0|65535|This defines the max number of retries if the PPP times out before sending another LCP configure request message. When this number is reached the PPP handshake is aborted and the link status is down. The default value is 20.
NX_MDNS_QUERY_DELAY_RANGE|NX_MDNS_QUERY_DELAY_RANGE|mDNS||0|2147483647|The delay range for sending first query, in ticks. The default value is 10 ticks for 100ms.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_PACKET_TIMEOUT|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_PACKET_TIMEOUT|SNTP||0|2147483647|Time out for NetX Duo packet allocation. The default NetX Duo SNTP Client packet timeout is 1 second.
NX_DISABLE_PACKET_CHAIN|NX_DISABLE_PACKET_CHAIN|Core||||Defined, disables the packet chain logic. By default this is not defined.
NXD_MQTT_PING_TIMEOUT_DELAY|NXD_MQTT_PING_TIMEOUT_DELAY|MQTT Client||0|2147483647|Defines the MQTT timer rate, in ThreadX timer ticks. This timer is used to keep track of the time since last MQTT control message was sent, and sends out an MQTT PINGREQ message before the keep-alive time expires. This timer is activated if the client connects to the broker with a keep-alive timer value set. The default value is TX_TIMER_TICKS_PER_SECOND, which is a one-second timer.
NX_MDNS_QUERY_DELAY_MIN|NX_MDNS_QUERY_DELAY_MIN|mDNS||0|2147483647|The minimum delay for sending first query, in ticks. The default value is 2 ticks for 20ms.
NX_AUTO_IP_DEFEND_INTERVAL|NX_AUTO_IP_DEFEND_INTERVAL|AUTO_IP||0|65535|The number of seconds to wait between defense announces. By default, this value is defined as 10.
NX_ENABLE_IP_STATIC_ROUTING|NX_ENABLE_IP_STATIC_ROUTING|IP||||Defined, enables IPv4 static routing in which a destination address can be assigned a specific next hop address. By default IPv4 static routing is disabled.
NX_ICMPV6_RTR_SOLICITATION_INTERVAL|NX_ICMPV6_RTR_SOLICITATION_INTERVAL|ICMP||0|65535|Specifies the interval between two router solicitation messages. The default value is 4.
NX_DHCPV6_DOMAIN_NAME_BUFFER_SIZE|NX_DHCPV6_DOMAIN_NAME_BUFFER_SIZE|DHCP||1|65535|Size of the buffer in the Client record to hold the client’s network domain name. The default value is 32.
NX_IP_MAX_REASSEMBLY_TIME|NX_IP_MAX_REASSEMBLY_TIME|IP||0|65535|Symbol that controls maximum time allowed to reassemble IPv4 fragment and IPv6 fragment. Note the value defined here overwrites both NX_IPV4_MAX_REASSEMBLY_TIME and NX_IPV6_MAX_REASSEMBLY_TIME.
NX_PPP_PPPOE_ENABLE|NX_PPP_PPPOE_ENABLE|PPP||||If defined, PPP can transmit packet over Ethernet.
NX_ARP_DEFEND_INTERVAL|NX_ARP_DEFEND_INTERVAL|ARP/RARP||0|65535|Defines the interval, in seconds, the ARP module sends out the next defend packet in response to an incoming ARP message that indicates an address in conflict.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_MIN_PACKET_SIZE|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_MIN_PACKET_SIZE|WEB Server||0|65535|Specifies the minimum size of the packets in the pool specified at server creation. The minimum size is needed to ensure the complete HTTP header can be contained in one packet. The default value is set to 600.
NXD_MQTT_SECURE_MEMCMP|NXD_MQTT_SECURE_MEMCMP|MQTT Client||||Define memcmp function used internal.
NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_REDIRECT_PROCESS|NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_REDIRECT_PROCESS|ICMP||||Defined, disables ICMPv6 redirect packet processing. NetX Duo by default processes redirect messages and updates the destination table with next hop IP address information.
NX_PPP_SERIAL_BUFFER_SIZE|NX_PPP_SERIAL_BUFFER_SIZE|PPP||1|2147483647|Specifies the size of the receive character serial buffer. By default, this value is 3,000 bytes. This define can be set by the application prior to inclusion of nx_ppp.h. By default, it is NX_PPP_MRU*2.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_TIME_TO_LIVE|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_TIME_TO_LIVE|SNTP||0x0|0xffffffff|Specifies the number of routers a Client packet can pass before it is discarded. The default NetX Duo SNTP Client is set to 0x80(NX_IP_TIME_TO_LIVE).
NX_TCP_KEEPALIVE_RETRIES|NX_TCP_KEEPALIVE_RETRIES|TCP||0|65535|Specifies how many keepalive retries are allowed before the connection is deemed broken. The default value is 10, which represents 10 retries, and is defined in nx_tcp.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_DISABLE_UDP_RX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_UDP_RX_CHECKSUM|UDP||||Defined, disables the UDP checksum computation on incoming UDP packets. This is useful if the network interface driver is able to verify UDP header checksum in hardware, and the application does not enable IPsec or IP fragmentation logic.
NX_DEBUG|NX_DEBUG|Core||||Defined, enables the optional print debug information available from the RAM Ethernet network driver.
NX_DHCP_ARP_PROBE_MAX|NX_DHCP_ARP_PROBE_MAX|DHCP||0|2147483647|Defines the maximum variation in the interval between sending ARP probes. The value is defaulted to 2 seconds.
NX_ENABLE_IP_RAW_PACKET_FILTER|NX_ENABLE_IP_RAW_PACKET_FILTER|IP||||Defined, enables the IP raw packet receive filter functionality. Applications requiring more control over the type of raw IP packets to be received can use this feature. The IP raw packet filter feature also supports the raw socket operation in the BSD compatibility layer. By default this option is not defined.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_RETRY_MAX|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_RETRY_MAX|WEB Server||0|65535|This sets the maximum number of retransmissions on Server socket. The default value is set to 10.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TIMEOUT|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TIMEOUT|WEB Server||0|65535|Specifies the number of ThreadX ticks that internal services will suspend for. The default value is set to 10 seconds (10 * NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_SUCCESS|NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_SUCCESS|DHCP||||This defines the status option message for : NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_SUCCESS. The default value is "IA OPTION GRANTED".
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_RETRY_SECONDS|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_RETRY_SECONDS|WEB Server||0|65535|Set the Server socket retransmission timeout in seconds. The default value is set to 2.
NX_WEB_HTTP_MAX_RESOURCE|NX_WEB_HTTP_MAX_RESOURCE|WEB Server||0|65535|Specifies the number of bytes allowed in a client supplied resource name. The default value is set to 40.
NX_PPP_PACKET|NX_PPP_PACKET|PPP||0|65535|Define the packet header.
NX_ARP_MAXIMUM_RETRIES|NX_ARP_MAXIMUM_RETRIES|ARP/RARP||0|65535|Specifies the maximum number of ARP retries made without an ARP response. The default value is 18 and is defined in nx_api.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_SLEEP_INTERVAL|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_SLEEP_INTERVAL|SNTP||0|65535|The time interval during which the SNTP Client task sleeps. This allows the application API calls to be executed by the SNTP Client. The default value is 1 timer tick.
NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_USE_DF|NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_USE_DF|CRYPTO DRBG||0|65535|This option define drbg use df.
NX_DNS_PACKET_POOL_SIZE|NX_DNS_PACKET_POOL_SIZE|DNS||1|2147483647|Size of the Client packet pool for sending DNS queries if NX_DNS_CLIENT_USER_CREATE_PACKET_POOL is not defined. The default value is large enough for 16 packets of payload size defined by NX_DNS_PACKET_PAYLOAD, and is 4-byte aligned. The default value is (16 * (NX_DNS_PACKET_PAYLOAD + sizeof(NX_PACKET))).
NX_DISABLE_IP_RX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_IP_RX_CHECKSUM|IP||||Defined, disables checksum logic on received IPv4 packets. This is useful if the network device is able to verify the IPv4 checksum, and the application does not expect to use IP fragmentation or IPsec.
NX_DNS_FRAGMENT_OPTION|NX_DNS_FRAGMENT_OPTION|DNS||||Sets the socket property to allow or disallow fragmentation of outgoing packets. The default value is NX_DONT_FRAGMENT.
NX_SECURE_TLS_ENABLE_TLS_1_1|NX_SECURE_TLS_ENABLE_TLS_1_1|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables the legacy TLSv1.1 mode. TLSv1.1 is considered obsolete so it should only be enabled for backward-compatibility with older applications.
NX_PPP_MRU|NX_PPP_MRU|PPP||0|2147483647|Specifies the Maximum Receive Unit (MRU) for PPP. By default, this value is 1,500 bytes (the minimum value). This define can be set by the application prior to inclusion of nx_ppp.h.
NX_IPV4_MAX_REASSEMBLY_TIME|NX_IPV4_MAX_REASSEMBLY_TIME|IP||0|65535|Symbol that controls maximum time allowed to reassemble IPv4 fragment. Note the value defined in NX_IP_MAX_REASSEMBLY_TIME overwrites this value. The default value is 15.
NX_SECURE_TLS_ENABLE_TLS_1_3|NX_SECURE_TLS_ENABLE_TLS_1_3|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables TLSv1.3 mode. TLS 1.3 is the newest version of TLS and is disabled by default.
NX_MDNS_POOF_TIMER_COUNT|NX_MDNS_POOF_TIMER_COUNT|mDNS||0|2147483647|Define the Passive Observation Of Failures timer count, 10 seconds in spec (10 * NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_MAX|NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_MAX|DHCP||1|65535|Defines the maximum size of the Server message in status option message field . The default value is 100 bytes.
NX_RETRANS_TIMER|NX_RETRANS_TIMER|Core||0|2147483647|Specifies in milliseconds the length of delay between solicitation packets sent by NetX Duo. Defined in nx_nd_cache.h, the default value is 1000.
NX_SECURE_TLS_TLS_1_3_ENABLED|NX_SECURE_TLS_TLS_1_3_ENABLED|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables TLS 1.3 .
NX_DHCPV6_TYPE_OF_SERVICE|NX_DHCPV6_TYPE_OF_SERVICE|DHCP||||This defines the type of service for UDP packet transmission from the DHCPv6 Client socket. The default value is NX_IP_NORMAL.
NX_ENABLE_IP_PACKET_FILTER|NX_ENABLE_IP_PACKET_FILTER|IP||||
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_MAX_PENDING|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_MAX_PENDING|WEB Server||0|65535|Specifies the number of connections that can be queued for the HTTPS Server. The default value is set to twice the maximum number of server sessions ((NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_SESSION_MAX << 1).
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_UNICAST_POLL_INTERVAL|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_UNICAST_POLL_INTERVAL|SNTP||0|65535|The starting poll interval (seconds) on which the Client sends a unicast request to its SNTP server. The NetX Duo SNTP Client default is 3600.
NX_DHCPV6_MAX_CLIENTS|NX_DHCPV6_MAX_CLIENTS|DHCP||1|65535|Defines the size of the Server’s Client record table (e.g. max number of Clients that can be stored). This value should be less than or equal to the value NX_DHCPV6_MAX_LEASES.By default, this value is 120.
NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_THREAD_PRIORITY|NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_THREAD_PRIORITY|DHCP||0|255|This defines the DHCPv6 Server thread priority. This should be lower than the DHCPv6 Server’s IP thread task priority. The default value is 2.
NX_MDNS_RR_TTL_OTHER|NX_MDNS_RR_TTL_OTHER|mDNS||0|65535|TTL value for other resource records, in second. The default value is 4500 for 75 minutes.
NX_CRYPTO_FIPS|NX_CRYPTO_FIPS|CRYPTO CORE||||Defined, this option enables extra security features required for FIPS-Compliant usage. This option is not enabled for non-FIPS build.
NX_MDNS_ANNOUNCING_TIMER_COUNT|NX_MDNS_ANNOUNCING_TIMER_COUNT|mDNS||0|2147483647|The time interval, in ticks, between mDNS announcement messages. The default value is 25 ticks for 250ms.
NX_DHCP_CLIENT_RESTORE_STATE|NX_DHCP_CLIENT_RESTORE_STATE|DHCP||||If defined, this enables the DHCP Client to save its current DHCP Client license ‘state’ including time remaining on the lease, and restore this state between DHCP Client application reboots. The default value is disabled.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MIN_TIME_ADJUSTMENT|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MIN_TIME_ADJUSTMENT|SNTP||0|2147483647|The minimum time adjustment in milliseconds the Client will make to its local clock time. Time adjustments below this will be ignored. The NetX Duo SNTP Client default is 10.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TRANSMIT_QUEUE_DEPTH|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TRANSMIT_QUEUE_DEPTH|WEB Server||0|65535|This specifies the maximum number of packets that can be enqueued on the Server socket retransmission queue. If the number of packets enqueued reaches this number, no more packets can be sent until one or more enqueued packets are released.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_WINDOW_SIZE|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_WINDOW_SIZE|WEB Server||0|65535|Server socket window size. By default, this value is 8192.
NX_MDNS_GOODBYE_TIMER_COUNT|NX_MDNS_GOODBYE_TIMER_COUNT|mDNS||0|2147483647|The time interval, in ticks, between repeated "goodbye" messages. The default value is 25 ticks for 250ms.
NX_TCP_KEEPALIVE_INITIAL|NX_TCP_KEEPALIVE_INITIAL|TCP||0|65535|Specifies the number of seconds of inactivity before the keepalive timer activates. The default value is 7200, which represents 2 hours, and is defined in nx_tcp.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_TCP_MAXIMUM_RX_QUEUE|NX_TCP_MAXIMUM_RX_QUEUE|TCP||0|65535|Symbol that defines the maximum receive queue for TCP sockets. This feature is enabled by NX_ENABLE_LOW_WATERMARK.
NX_DNS_MAX_SERVERS|NX_DNS_MAX_SERVERS|DNS||1|65535|Specifies the maximum number of DNS Servers in the Client server list. The default value is 5.
NX_TCP_MAXIMUM_TX_QUEUE|NX_TCP_MAXIMUM_TX_QUEUE|TCP||0|65535|Specifies the maximum depth of the TCP transmit queue before TCP send requests are suspended or rejected. The default value is 20, which means that a maximum of 20 packets can be in the transmit queue at any given time. Note packets stay in the transmit queue until an ACK that covers some or all of the packet data is received from the other side of the connection. This constant is defined in nx_tcp.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_PPP_DNS_ADDRESS_MAX_RETRIES|NX_PPP_DNS_ADDRESS_MAX_RETRIES|PPP||0|65535|This specifies how many times the PPP host will request a DNS Server address from the peer in the IPCP state. This has no effect if NX_PPP_DNS_OPTION_DISABLE is defined. The default value is 2.
NX_SECURE_DTLS_RETRANSMIT_RETRY_SHIFT|NX_SECURE_DTLS_RETRANSMIT_RETRY_SHIFT|DTLS CORE||0|2147483647|This option defines how the retransmit timeout period changes between successive retries. If this value is 0, the initial retransmit timeout is the same as subsequent retransmit timeouts. If this value is 1, each successive retransmit is twice as long.
NX_DHCP_DEFAULT_LEASE_TIME|NX_DHCP_DEFAULT_LEASE_TIME|DHCP||0|2147483647|This is IP Address lease time in seconds assigned to the DHCP Client, and the basis for computing the renewal and rebind times also assigned to the Client. The default value is set to (10 * NX_DHCP_SLOW_PERIODIC_TIME_INTERVAL).
NX_PPP_DEBUG_FRAME_SIZE|NX_PPP_DEBUG_FRAME_SIZE|PPP||1|65535|Maximum amount of data captured from a received packet payload and saved to debug output. The default value is 50.
NX_DHCP_QUEUE_DEPTH|NX_DHCP_QUEUE_DEPTH|DHCP||0|65535|Specifies the number of maximum depth of receive queue. The default value is set to 4.
NX_SECURE_X509_STRICT_NAME_COMPARE|NX_SECURE_X509_STRICT_NAME_COMPARE|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables strict distinguished name comparison for X.509 certificates for certificate searching and verification. The default is to only compare the Common Name fields of the Distinguished Names.
NX_DHCPV6_TIME_ZONE_BUFFER_SIZE|NX_DHCPV6_TIME_ZONE_BUFFER_SIZE|DHCP||1|65535|Size of the buffer in the Client record to hold the Client’s time zone. The default value is 16.
NXD_MQTT_CLIENT_THREAD_TIME_SLICE|NXD_MQTT_CLIENT_THREAD_TIME_SLICE|MQTT Client||0|65535|Define the default MQTT Thread time slice.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_UDP_SOCKET_NAME|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_UDP_SOCKET_NAME|SNTP||||This option sets the UDP socket name. The NetX Duo SNTP Client UDP socket name default is “SNTP Client socket.”.
NX_PPP_TIMEOUT|NX_PPP_TIMEOUT|PPP||0|2147483647|This defines the wait option (in timer ticks) for allocating packets to transmit data as well as buffer PPP serial data into packets to send to the IP layer. The default value is 4*NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE (400 ticks).
NX_DISABLE_RARP_INFO|NX_DISABLE_RARP_INFO|ARP/RARP||||Defined, disables RARP information gathering.
NX_SECURE_X509_PARSE_CRL_EXTENSION|NX_SECURE_X509_PARSE_CRL_EXTENSION|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables X509 parse crl extension.
NX_MDNS_DOMAIN_NAME_MAX|NX_MDNS_DOMAIN_NAME_MAX|mDNS||5|65535|Maximum string size for domain name. The default value is 16. Does not include the NULL terminator. <font color="red"> <b>(NX_MDNS_HOST_NAME_MAX + 1 + NX_MDNS_DOMAIN_NAME_MAX) must be no more than NX_MDNS_NAME_MAX! </b> </font>
UX_MAX_SLAVE_CLASS_DRIVER|UX_MAX_SLAVE_CLASS_DRIVER|Device Core||0|255|This value is the maximum number of classes in the device stack that can be loaded by USBX
NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_DUID_TYPE|NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_DUID_TYPE|DHCP||||This defines the Server DUID type which the Server includes in all messages to Clients. The default value is link layer plus time (NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_DUID_TYPE_LINK_TIME).
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TIMEOUT_DISCONNECT|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TIMEOUT_DISCONNECT|WEB Server||0|2147483647|Specifies the number of ThreadX ticks that internal services will suspend for in internal nx_tcp_socket_disconnect() calls. The default value is set to 10 seconds (10 * NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NX_DHCPV6_IP_LIFETIME_TIMER_INTERVAL|NX_DHCPV6_IP_LIFETIME_TIMER_INTERVAL|DHCP||0|65535|Time interval in seconds at which the IP lifetime timer updates the length of time the current IP address has been assigned to the Client. By default, this value is 1.
NX_DHCPV6_SESSION_TIMER_INTERVAL|NX_DHCPV6_SESSION_TIMER_INTERVAL|DHCP||0|65535|Time interval in seconds at which the session timer updates the length of time the Client has been in session communicating with the Server. By default, this value is 1.
NX_ARP_UPDATE_RATE|NX_ARP_UPDATE_RATE|ARP/RARP||0|65535|Specifies the number of seconds between ARP retries. The default value is 10, which represents 10 seconds, and is defined in nx_api.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_MDNS_HOST_NAME_MAX|NX_MDNS_HOST_NAME_MAX|mDNS||0|65535|Maximum string size for host name. The default value is 64. Does not include the NULL terminator. <font color="red"> <b>(NX_MDNS_HOST_NAME_MAX + 1 + NX_MDNS_DOMAIN_NAME_MAX) must be no more than NX_MDNS_NAME_MAX! </b> </font>
NX_SECURE_POWER_ON_SELF_TEST_MODULE_INTEGRITY_CHECK|NX_SECURE_POWER_ON_SELF_TEST_MODULE_INTEGRITY_CHECK|TLS CORE||||This option enables module integrity self test.
NX_DHCPV6_MAX_OPTION_REQUEST_OPTIONS|NX_DHCPV6_MAX_OPTION_REQUEST_OPTIONS|DHCP||1|65535|This defines the maximum number of option requests in a Client request that can be saved to a Client record. The default value is 6.
NX_DHCP_CLIENT_ENABLE_HOST_NAME_CHECK|NX_DHCP_CLIENT_ENABLE_HOST_NAME_CHECK|DHCP||||Defined, this enables the DHCP Client to check the input host name in the nx_dhcp_create call for invalid characters or length. By default, this option is disabled.
NX_DHCPV6_PACKET_SIZE|NX_DHCPV6_PACKET_SIZE|DHCP||0|65535|This defines the packet payload of the Server packet pool packets. The default value is 500 bytes.
NX_PPP_DISABLE_INFO|NX_PPP_DISABLE_INFO|PPP||||If defined, internal PPP information gathering is disabled.
NX_MDNS_GOODBYE_RETRANSMIT_COUNT|NX_MDNS_GOODBYE_RETRANSMIT_COUNT|mDNS||0|65535|The number of retransmitted "goodbye" messages. The default value is 1.
NX_MAX_PHYSICAL_INTERFACES|NX_MAX_PHYSICAL_INTERFACES|Core||1|255|Specifies the total number of physical network interfaces on the device. The default value is 1 and is defined in nx_api.h; a device must have at least one physical interface. Note this does not include the loopback interface.
NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_TX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_TX_CHECKSUM|ICMP||||Defined, disables and ICMPv6 checksum computation on transmitted ICMP packets.
NX_DISABLE_ICMPV4_ERROR_MESSAGE|NX_DISABLE_ICMPV4_ERROR_MESSAGE|ICMP||||Defined, NetX Duo does not send ICMPv4 Error Messages in response to error conditions such as improperly formatted IPv4 header. By default this option is not defined.
NX_DISABLE_ARP_AUTO_ENTRY|NX_DISABLE_ARP_AUTO_ENTRY|ARP/RARP||||Defined, disables entering ARP request information in the ARP cache.
NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_SHARED_DELAY_RANGE|NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_SHARED_DELAY_RANGE|mDNS||0|2147483647|The delay range, in ticks, in responding to a query to a shared resource. The default value is 10 ticks for 100ms.
NX_DNS_MAX_RETRIES|NX_DNS_MAX_RETRIES|DNS||0|255|The maximum number of times the DNS Client will query the current DNS server before trying another server or aborting the DNS query. The default value is 3.
NX_CRYPTO_MAX_RSA_MODULUS_SIZE|NX_CRYPTO_MAX_RSA_MODULUS_SIZE|CRYPTO CORE||||Defined, this option gives the maximum RSA modulus expected, in bits. The default value is 4096 for a 4096-bit modulus. Other values can be 3072, 2048, or 1024 (not recommended).
NX_PPP_MAX_CHAP_PROTOCOL_RETRIES|NX_PPP_MAX_CHAP_PROTOCOL_RETRIES|PPP||0|65535|This defines the max number of retries if the PPP times out before sending another CHAP challenge message. When this number is reached the PPP handshake is aborted and the link status is down. The default value is 20.
NX_SECURE_X509_DISABLE_CRL|NX_SECURE_X509_DISABLE_CRL|TLS CORE||||This option disables X509 Certificate Revocation List check.
NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_ROUTER_SOLICITATION|NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_ROUTER_SOLICITATION|ICMP||||Defined, disables NetX Duo from sending IPv6 router solicitation messages at regular intervals to the router.
NX_PPP_HASHED_VALUE_SIZE|NX_PPP_HASHED_VALUE_SIZE|PPP||0|65535|Specifies the size of “hashed value” strings used in CHAP authentication. The default value is set to 16 bytes, but can be redefined prior to inclusion of nx_ppp.h.
NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_MAX_SEED_LIFE|NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_MAX_SEED_LIFE|CRYPTO DRBG||0|2147483647|This option defines the drbg max seed life. The default value is 100000.
NX_DHCPV6_DEFAULT_PREFERRED_TIME|NX_DHCPV6_DEFAULT_PREFERRED_TIME|DHCP||0|65535|This defines the time in seconds assigned bythe Server for when an assigned Client IP address lease is deprecated. The default value is 2 NX_DHCPV6_DEFAULT_T1_TIME.
NXD_MQTT_CLOUD_ENABLE|NXD_MQTT_CLOUD_ENABLE|MQTT Client||||Defined, enable MQTT over cloud option.
NX_DHCP_FRAGMENT_OPTION|NX_DHCP_FRAGMENT_OPTION|DHCP||||Fragment enable for DHCP UDP requests. By default, this value is NX_DONT_FRAGMENT to disable DHCP UDP fragmenting.
NX_ENABLE_INTERFACE_CAPABILITY|NX_ENABLE_INTERFACE_CAPABILITY|Core||||Defined, allows the interface device driver to specify extra capability information, such as checksum off-loading. By default this option is not defined.
NX_DISABLE_IPV4|NX_DISABLE_IPV4|IP||||Defined, disables IPv4 functionality. This option can be used to build NetX Duo to suupport IPv6 only. By default this option is not defined. <font color="red"> NX_DISABLE_IPV4 and NX_DISABLE_IPV6 are mutually exclusive: either IPv4 or IPv6 must be enabled </font>
NX_DISABLE_IPV6|NX_DISABLE_IPV6|IP||||Disables IPv6 functionality when the NetX Duo library is built. For applications that do not need IPv6, this avoids pulling in code and additional storage space needed to support IPv6. <font color="red"> NX_DISABLE_IPV4 and NX_DISABLE_IPV6 are mutually exclusive: either IPv4 or IPv6 must be enabled </font>
NX_ENABLE_IPV6_PATH_MTU_DISCOVERY|NX_ENABLE_IPV6_PATH_MTU_DISCOVERY|IP||||Defined, enables the IPv6 path MTU discovery feature. By default this option is not enabled.
NX_DHCPV6_IP_LEASE_TIMER_INTERVAL|NX_DHCPV6_IP_LEASE_TIMER_INTERVAL|DHCP||0|65535|Timer interval in seconds when the lease timer entry function is called by the ThreadX scheduler. The entry function sets a flag for the DHCPv6 Server to increment all Clients’ accrued time on their lease by the timer interval. By default, this value is 60.
NX_WEB_HTTP_TIME_TO_LIVE|NX_WEB_HTTP_TIME_TO_LIVE|WEB Server||0x0|0xffffffff|Specifies the number of routers this packet can pass before it is discarded. The default value is set to 0x80.
NX_DISABLE_IP_TX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_IP_TX_CHECKSUM|IP||||Defined, disables checksum logic on IPv4 packets sent. This is useful in situations in which the underlying network device is capable of generating the IPv4 header checksum, and the application does not expect to use IP fragmentation or IPsec.
NX_CRYPTO_HARDWARE_RAND_INITIALIZE|NX_CRYPTO_HARDWARE_RAND_INITIALIZE|CRYPTO CORE||||Defined, this option enables crypto hardware random initialize.
NX_DHCPV6_PREFERENCE_VALUE|NX_DHCPV6_PREFERENCE_VALUE|DHCP||0|65535|This defines the preference option value between 0 and 255, where the higher the value the higher the preference, in the DHCPv6 option of the same name. This tells the Client what preference to place on this Server’s offer where multiple DHCPv6 Servers are available to assign IP addresses. A value of 255 instructs the Client to choose this server. A value of zero indicates the Client is free to choose. The default value is zero.
NX_PPP_MINIMUM_MRU|NX_PPP_MINIMUM_MRU|PPP||0|2147483647|Specifies the minimum MRU received in an LCP configure request message. By default, this value is 1,500 bytes (the minimum value). This define can be set by the application prior to inclusion of nx_ppp.h.
NXD_MQTT_SECURE_MEMSET|NXD_MQTT_SECURE_MEMSET|MQTT Client||||Define memset function used internal.
NX_SNTP_CURRENT_YEAR|NX_SNTP_CURRENT_YEAR|SNTP||0|65535|To display date in year/month/date format, set this value to equal or less than current year (need not be same year as in NTP time being evaluated). The default value is 2015.
NX_SECURE_TLS_TLS_1_2_ENABLED|NX_SECURE_TLS_TLS_1_2_ENABLED|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables TLS 1.2 .
NX_CRYPTO_ECDH_SCRATCH_BUFFER_SIZE|NX_CRYPTO_ECDH_SCRATCH_BUFFER_SIZE|CRYPTO ECDH||1|65535|This option defines ecdh scratch buffer size.
NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_RX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_RX_CHECKSUM|ICMP||||Defined, disables ICMPv6 checksum computation on received ICMP packets.
NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_DUID_VENDOR_ASSIGNED_LENGTH|NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_DUID_VENDOR_ASSIGNED_LENGTH|DHCP||1|255|Sets the upper limit on the Vendor assigned ID. The default value is 48.
NX_PPP_PROTOCOL_TIMEOUT|NX_PPP_PROTOCOL_TIMEOUT|PPP||0|65535|This defines the wait option (in seconds) for the PPP task to receive a response to a PPP protocol request message. The default value is 4 seconds.
NX_DHCPV6_QUEUE_DEPTH|NX_DHCPV6_QUEUE_DEPTH|DHCP||0|65535|Specifies the number of packets to keep in the Client UDP socket receive queue before NetX Duo discards packets. The default value is 5.
NX_WEB_HTTP_MULTIPART_ENABLE|NX_WEB_HTTP_MULTIPART_ENABLE|WEB Server||||If defined, enables HTTPS Server to support multipart HTTP requests.
NX_DRIVER_DEFERRED_PROCESSING|NX_DRIVER_DEFERRED_PROCESSING|Core||||Defined, enables deferred network driver packet handling. This allows the network driver to place a packet on the IP instance and have the real processing routine called from the NetX Duo internal IP helper thread.
NX_SECURE_TLS_MAX_PSK_KEYS|NX_SECURE_TLS_MAX_PSK_KEYS|TLS CORE||1|2147483647|This option defines the maximum PSK keys.
NX_DHCP_TIME_TO_LIVE|NX_DHCP_TIME_TO_LIVE|DHCP||0|65535|Specifies the number of routers this packet can pass before it is discarded. The default value is set to 0x80.
NX_DNS_CACHE_ENABLE|NX_DNS_CACHE_ENABLE|DNS||||This enables the DNS Client to store the answer records into DNS cache.
NX_WEB_HTTPS_ENABLE|NX_WEB_HTTPS_ENABLE|WEB Server||||If defined, this macro enables TLS and HTTPS. Leave undefined to free up resources if only plaintext HTTP is desired. By default, this macro is not defined.
NX_WEB_HTTP_DIGEST_ENABLE|NX_WEB_HTTP_DIGEST_ENABLE|WEB Server||||If defined, authentication using the MD5 digest is enabled on the HTTPS Server. By default it is not defined.
NX_ENABLE_IPV6_ADDRESS_CHANGE_NOTIFY|NX_ENABLE_IPV6_ADDRESS_CHANGE_NOTIFY|IP||||Defined, allows a callback function to be invoked when the IPv6 address is changed. By default this option is not enabled.
NX_MDNS_QUERY_MIN_TIMER_COUNT|NX_MDNS_QUERY_MIN_TIMER_COUNT|mDNS||0|2147483647|The minimum time interval, in ticks, between two queries. The default value is 100 ticks for 1 second.
NX_PPP_MIN_PACKET_PAYLOAD|NX_PPP_MIN_PACKET_PAYLOAD|PPP||0|65535|Define the minimum PPP packet payload, the PPP commands (LCP, PAP, CHAP, IPCP) should be in one packet. The default value is (NX_PPP_PACKET + 128).
NX_SECURE_TLS_MAX_PSK_NONCE_SIZE|NX_SECURE_TLS_MAX_PSK_NONCE_SIZE|TLS CORE||1|65535|This option defines the TLS maximum psk monce size. The default value is 255.
NX_MAX_STRING_LENGTH|NX_MAX_STRING_LENGTH|Core||0|65535|Define the max string length.
NX_ARP_EXPIRATION_RATE|NX_ARP_EXPIRATION_RATE|ARP/RARP||0|65535|Specifies the number of seconds ARP entries remain valid. The default value of zero disables expiration or aging of ARP entries and is defined in nx_api.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_ENABLE_TCP_KEEPALIVE|NX_ENABLE_TCP_KEEPALIVE|TCP||||Defined, enables the optional TCP keepalive timer. The default settings is not enabled.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_IGNORE_MAX_ADJUST_STARTUP|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_IGNORE_MAX_ADJUST_STARTUP|SNTP||||This enables the maximum time adjustment to be waived when the Client receives the first update from its time server. Thereafter, the maximum time adjustment is enforced. The intention is to get the Client in synch with the server clock as soon as possible. The NetX Duo SNTP Client default is NX_TRUE.
NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_SHARED_DELAY_MIN|NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_SHARED_DELAY_MIN|mDNS||0|2147483647|The minimum delay, in ticks, in responding to a query to a shared resource. The default value is 2 ticks for 20ms.
NTP_SECONDS_AT_01011999|NTP_SECONDS_AT_01011999|SNTP||0x0|0xFFFFFFFF|This is the number of seconds into the first NTP Epoch on the master NTP clock. It is defined as 0xBA368E80. To disable display of NTP seconds into date and time, set to zero.
NX_DISABLE_PACKET_INFO|NX_DISABLE_PACKET_INFO|IP||||Defined, disables packet pool information gathering.
NX_DNS_MESSAGE_MAX|NX_DNS_MESSAGE_MAX|DNS||0|512|The maximum DNS message size for sending DNS queries. The default value is 512, which is also the maximum size specified in RFC 1035 Section 2.3.4.
NX_TCP_IMMEDIATE_ACK|NX_TCP_IMMEDIATE_ACK|TCP||||Defined, enables the optional TCP immediate ACK response processing. Defining this symbol is equivalent to defining NX_TCP_ACK_EVERY_N_PACKETS to be 1.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TIMEOUT_RECEIVE|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TIMEOUT_RECEIVE|WEB Server||0|2147483647|Specifies the number of ThreadX ticks that internal services will suspend for in internal nx_tcp_socket_receive() calls. The default value is set to 10 seconds (10 * NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NX_SECURE_X509_USE_EXTENDED_DISTINGUISHED_NAMES|NX_SECURE_X509_USE_EXTENDED_DISTINGUISHED_NAMES|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables the optional X.509 Distinguished Name fields, at the expense of extra memory use for X.509 certificates.
NX_DHCP_ARP_PROBE_MIN|NX_DHCP_ARP_PROBE_MIN|DHCP||0|2147483647|Defines the minimum variation in the interval between sending ARP probes. The value is defaulted to 1 second.
NX_SECURE_ENABLE_DTLS|NX_SECURE_ENABLE_DTLS|DTLS CORE||||This macro must be defined to enable DTLS logic in NetX Secure.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_EXP_BACKOFF_RATE|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_EXP_BACKOFF_RATE|SNTP||0|65535|The factor by which the current Client unicast poll interval is increased. When the Client fails to receive a server time update, or receiving indications from the server that it is temporarily unavailable (e.g. not synchronized yet) for time update service, it will increase the current poll interval by this rate up to but not exceeding NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MAX_TIME_LAPSE. The default is 2.
NX_MDNS_CONFLICT_COUNT|NX_MDNS_CONFLICT_COUNT|mDNS||0|65535|Maximum conflict count for host name or service name. The default value is 8.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH|SNTP||0|65535|Maximum number of UDP packets (datagrams) that can be queued in the NetX Duo SNTP Client socket. Additional packets received mean the oldest packets are released. The default NetX Duo SNTP Client is set to 5.
NX_DHCP_SERVER_THREAD_PRIORITY|NX_DHCP_SERVER_THREAD_PRIORITY|DHCP||0|255|This option specifies the priority of the DHCP Server thread. By default, this value specifies that the DHCP thread runs at priority 2.
NX_DISABLE_FRAGMENTATION|NX_DISABLE_FRAGMENTATION|IP||||Defined, disables both IPv4 and IPv6 fragmentation and reassembly logic. If checked, the parameter NX_DISABLE_PACKET_CHAIN will be available.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MIN_SERVER_STRATUM|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MIN_SERVER_STRATUM|SNTP||1|15|The lowest level (highest numeric stratum level) SNTP Server stratum the Client will accept. The NetX Duo SNTP Client default is 2.
NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_USE_MULTICAST|NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_USE_MULTICAST|DHCP||||This defines the status option message for : NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_USE_MULTICAST. The default value is "IA OPTION NOT GRANTED-CLIENT MUST USE MULTICAST".
NX_ENABLE_ARP_MAC_CHANGE_NOTIFICATION|NX_ENABLE_ARP_MAC_CHANGE_NOTIFICATION|ARP/RARP||||Defined, allows ARP to invoke a callback notify function on detecting the MAC address is updated.
NX_DHCP_CLIENT_MAX_RECORDS|NX_DHCP_CLIENT_MAX_RECORDS|DHCP||1|65535|Specifies the maximum number of interface records to save to the DHCP Client instance. A DHCP Client interface record is a record of the DHCP Client running on a specific interface. The default value is set as physical interfaces count (NX_MAX_PHYSICAL_INTERFACES).
NX_DISABLE_ERROR_CHECKING|NX_DISABLE_ERROR_CHECKING|Core||||Defined, removes the basic NetX Duo error checking API and improves performance. API return codes not affected by disabling error checking are listed in bold typeface in the API definition. This define is typically used after the application is debugged sufficiently and its use improves performance and decreases code size.
NX_CRYPTO_ECJPAKE_SCRATCH_BUFFER_SIZE|NX_CRYPTO_ECJPAKE_SCRATCH_BUFFER_SIZE|CRYPTO CORE||1|65535|This option defines the ecjpake scratch buffer size.
NX_SECURE_ENABLE_ECC_CIPHERSUITE|NX_SECURE_ENABLE_ECC_CIPHERSUITE|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables the ECC support in TLS.
NX_DHCP_ENABLE_BOOTP|NX_DHCP_ENABLE_BOOTP|DHCP||||Defined, this option enables the BOOTP protocol instead of DHCP. By default this option is disabled.
NX_IP_FAST_TIMER_RATE|NX_IP_FAST_TIMER_RATE|IP||0|65535|
NX_SECURE_ALLOW_SELF_SIGNED_CERTIFICATES|NX_SECURE_ALLOW_SELF_SIGNED_CERTIFICATES|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option allows TLS to accept self-signed certificates from a remote host. By default, TLS will reject self-signed server certificates as a security precaution. If this macro is defined, self-signed certificates must still be added to the trusted store to be accepted.
NX_WEB_HTTP_FRAGMENT_OPTION|NX_WEB_HTTP_FRAGMENT_OPTION|WEB Server||||Fragment enable for HTTP TCP requests. By default, this value is NX_DONT_FRAGMENT to disable HTTP TCP fragmenting.
NX_SECURE_ENABLE_CLIENT_CERTIFICATE_VERIFY|NX_SECURE_ENABLE_CLIENT_CERTIFICATE_VERIFY|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables the optional X.509 Client Certificate Verification for TLS Servers4.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_PRIORITY|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_PRIORITY|WEB Server||0|65535|The priority of the HTTPS Server thread. By default, this value is defined as 4 to specify priority 4.
NX_MAX_UNICAST_SOLICIT|NX_MAX_UNICAST_SOLICIT|Core||0|65535|Specifies the number of Neighbor Solicitation messages NetX Duo transmits to determine a specific neighbor's reachability. Defined in nx_nd_cache.h, the default value is 3.
NX_DHCP_PACKET_ALLOCATE_TIMEOUT|NX_DHCP_PACKET_ALLOCATE_TIMEOUT|DHCP||0|2147483647|Specifies the timeout in timer ticks for the NetX DHCP Server to wait for allocate a packet from its packet pool. The default value is set to NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MAX_ROOT_DISPERSION|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MAX_ROOT_DISPERSION|SNTP||0|2147483647|The maximum server clock dispersion (microseconds), which is a measure of server clock precision, the Client will accept. To disable this requirement, set the maximum root dispersion to 0x0. The NetX Duo SNTP Client default is set to 50000.
NX_ASSERT_FAIL|NX_ASSERT_FAIL|Core||||Symbol that defines the debug statement to use when an assertion fails.
NX_IPV6_DEFAULT_ROUTER_TABLE_SIZE|NX_IPV6_DEFAULT_ROUTER_TABLE_SIZE|IP||1|65535|Specifies the number of entries in the IPv6 routing table. At least one entry is needed for the default router. Defined in nx_api.h, the default value is 8.
NX_IP_RAW_MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH|NX_IP_RAW_MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH|IP||0|65535|Symbol that controls the number of raw IP packets can be queued on the raw packet receive queue. By default value is set to 20.
NX_PPP_DEBUG_LOG_PRINT_ENABLE|NX_PPP_DEBUG_LOG_PRINT_ENABLE|PPP||||If defined, internal PPP debug log printf to stdio is enabled. This is only valid if the debug log is also enabled.
NX_SECURE_MEMCMP|NX_SECURE_MEMCMP|TLS CORE||||This option defines the memory compare function.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_UDP_PORT|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_UDP_PORT|SNTP||0|65535|This sets the port which the Client socket is bound to. The default NetX Duo SNTP Client port is 123.
NX_SECURE_TLS_MAX_PSK_SIZE|NX_SECURE_TLS_MAX_PSK_SIZE|TLS CORE||1|2147483647|This option defines the maximum size of PSK.
NX_IPV6_DAD_TRANSMITS|NX_IPV6_DAD_TRANSMITS|IP||0|65535|Specifies the number of Neighbor Solicitation messages to be sent before NetX Duo marks an interface address as valid. If NX_DISABLE_IPV6_DAD is defined (DAD disabled), setting this option has no effect. Alternatively, a value of zero (0) turns off DAD but leaves the DAD functionality in NetX Duo. Defined in nx_api.h, the default value is 3.
NX_DHCP_MIN_RETRANS_TIMEOUT|NX_DHCP_MIN_RETRANS_TIMEOUT|DHCP||0|2147483647|Specifies the minimum wait option for receiving a DHCP Server reply to client message before retransmitting the message. The default value is the RFC 2131 recommended 4 seconds.
NX_WEB_HTTP_TYPE_OF_SERVICE|NX_WEB_HTTP_TYPE_OF_SERVICE|WEB Server||||Type of service required for the HTTPS TCP requests. By default, this value is defined as NX_IP_NORMAL to indicate normal IP packet service.
NX_ENABLE_IPV6_MULTICAST|NX_ENABLE_IPV6_MULTICAST|IP||||Defined, enables IPv6 multicast join/leave function. By default this option is not enabled.
NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_NO_BINDING|NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_NO_BINDING|DHCP||||This defines the status option message for : NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_NO_BINDING. The default value is "IA OPTION NOT GRANTED-INVALID CLIENT REQUEST".
NX_SECURE_ENABLE|NX_SECURE_ENABLE|MQTT Client||||When defined, MQTT Client is built with TLS support. Defining this symbol requires NetX Secure TLS module to be enabled. NX_SECURE_ENABLE is not enabled by default.
NX_DHCPV6_DEFAULT_VALID_TIME|NX_DHCPV6_DEFAULT_VALID_TIME|DHCP||0|65535|This defines the time expiration in seconds assigned by the Server on an assigned Client IP address lease. After this time expires, the Client IP address is invalid. The default value is 2 NX_DHCPV6_DEFAULT_PREFERRED_TIME.
NX_AUTO_IP_PROBE_MAX|NX_AUTO_IP_PROBE_MAX|AUTO_IP||0|65535|The maximum number of seconds to wait between sending probes. By default, this value is defined as 2.
NXD_MQTT_SECURE_MEMMOVE|NXD_MQTT_SECURE_MEMMOVE|MQTT Client||||Define memmove function used internal.
NX_DHCPV6_DEFAULT_T1_TIME|NX_DHCPV6_DEFAULT_T1_TIME|DHCP||0|65535|The time in seconds assigned by the Server on a Client address lease for when the Client should begin renewing its IP address. The default value is 2000 seconds.
NX_DHCP_ARP_PROBE_WAIT|NX_DHCP_ARP_PROBE_WAIT|DHCP||0|2147483647|Defines the length of time the DHCP Client waits for a response after sending an ARP probe. The default value is one second (1 * NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NX_SECURE_TLS_SERVER_DISABLED|NX_SECURE_TLS_SERVER_DISABLED|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option removes all TLS stack code related to TLS Server mode, reducing code and data usage.
NX_DISABLE_IPV6_PURGE_UNUSED_CACHE_ENTRIES|NX_DISABLE_IPV6_PURGE_UNUSED_CACHE_ENTRIES|IP||||Defined, this option prevents NetX Duo from removing older cache table entries before their timeout expires to make room for new entries when the table is full. Static and router entries are never purged.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MAX_TIME_LAPSE|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MAX_TIME_LAPSE|SNTP||0|65535|Maximum allowable amount of time (seconds) elapsed without a valid time update received by the SNTP Client. The SNTP Client will continue in operation but the SNTP Server status is set to NX_FALSE. The default value is 7200.
NXD_MQTT_CLIENT_SOCKET_WINDOW_SIZE|NXD_MQTT_CLIENT_SOCKET_WINDOW_SIZE|MQTT Client||0|65535|Define the default TCP socket window size.
NX_DNS_TIME_TO_LIVE|NX_DNS_TIME_TO_LIVE|DNS||0x0|0xffff|Specifies the maximum number of routers a packet can pass before it is discarded. The default value is 0x80.
FEATURE_NX_IPV6|FEATURE_NX_IPV6|IP||||Defined, enable IPV6 features.
NX_MDNS_SERVICE_NAME_MAX|NX_MDNS_SERVICE_NAME_MAX|mDNS||0|65535|Maximum string size for service name. The default value is 64. Does not include the NULL terminator.
NX_DHCPV6_NUM_DNS_SERVERS|NX_DHCPV6_NUM_DNS_SERVERS|DHCP||1|65535|Number of DNS servers to store to the client record. The default value is 2.
NX_AUTO_IP_MAX_CONFLICTS|NX_AUTO_IP_MAX_CONFLICTS|AUTO_IP||0|65535|The number of AutoIP conflicts before increasing processing delays. By default, this value is defined as 10.
NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_MAX_ENTROPY_LEN|NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_MAX_ENTROPY_LEN|CRYPTO DRBG||0|65535|This option defines the drbg max entropy length. The default value is 125.
NX_ICMPV6_RTR_SOLICITATION_DELAY|NX_ICMPV6_RTR_SOLICITATION_DELAY|ICMP||0|65535|Specifies the maximum delay for the initial router solicitation in seconds.
NX_SECURE_TLS_MAX_PSK_ID_SIZE|NX_SECURE_TLS_MAX_PSK_ID_SIZE|TLS CORE||1|2147483647|This option defines the maximum size of PSK ID.
NX_DISABLE_RESET_DISCONNECT|NX_DISABLE_RESET_DISCONNECT|TCP||||Defined, disables the reset processing during disconnect when the timeout value supplied is specified as NX_NO_WAIT.
NX_PPP_RECEIVE_TIMEOUTS|NX_PPP_RECEIVE_TIMEOUTS|PPP||0|65535|This defines the number of times the PPP thread task times out waiting to receive the next character in a PPP message stream. Thereafter, PPP releases the packet and begins waiting to receive the next PPP message. The default value is 4.
NX_ARP_DEFEND_BY_REPLY|NX_ARP_DEFEND_BY_REPLY|ARP/RARP||||Defined, allows NetX Duo to defend its IP address by sending an ARP response.
NX_SECURE_KEY_CLEAR|NX_SECURE_KEY_CLEAR|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables key related materials cleanup when they are not used anymore.
NX_IPV6_MAX_REASSEMBLY_TIME|NX_IPV6_MAX_REASSEMBLY_TIME|IP||0|65535|Symbol that controls the maximum time allowed to reassemble IPv6 fragment.
NX_MAX_IPV6_ADDRESSES|NX_MAX_IPV6_ADDRESSES|IP||0|1000|Specifies the number of entries in the IPv6 address pool. During interface configuration, NetX Duo uses IPv6 entries from the pool. It is defaulted to (NX_MAX_PHYSICAL_INTERFACES * 3) to allow each interface to have at least one link local address and two global addresses. Note that all interfaces share the IPv6 address pool.
NX_TCP_RETRY_SHIFT|NX_TCP_RETRY_SHIFT|TCP||0x0|0xF|Specifies how the retransmit timeout period changes between retries. If this value is 0, the initial retransmit timeout is the same as subsequent retransmit timeouts. If this value is 1, each successive retransmit is twice as long. If this value is 2, each subsequent retransmit timeout is four times as long. The default value is 0 and is defined in nx_tcp.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_DHCPV6_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE|NX_DHCPV6_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE|DHCP||1|65535|Size of the buffer in the Client record to hold the option status message in a Server reply. The default value is 100 bytes.
NX_MDNS_PROBING_TIMER_COUNT|NX_MDNS_PROBING_TIMER_COUNT|mDNS||0|2147483647|The time interval, in ticks, between mDNS probing messages. The default value is 25 ticks for 250ms.
NX_DHCPV6_PACKET_WAIT_OPTION|NX_DHCPV6_PACKET_WAIT_OPTION|DHCP||0|2147483647|This defines the wait option for the Server nx_udp_socket_receive call. This is perfunctory since the socket has a receive notify callback from NetX Duo, so the packet is already enqueued when the DHCPv6 server calls the receive function. The default value is 1 second (1 * NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NX_PATH_MTU_INCREASE_WAIT_INTERVAL|NX_PATH_MTU_INCREASE_WAIT_INTERVAL|IP||0|65535|Specifies the wait interval in timer ticks to reset the path MTU for a specific target in the destination table. If NX_DISABLE_IPV6_PATH_MTU_DISCOVERY is defined, defining this symbol has no effect.
NX_DISABLE_ICMP_INFO|NX_DISABLE_ICMP_INFO|ICMP||||Defined, disables ICMP information gathering.
NX_MDNS_TIMER_COUNT_RANGE|NX_MDNS_TIMER_COUNT_RANGE|mDNS||0|2147483647|When sending out mDNS responses, the packet contains responses that otherwise would be sent within this timer counter range. The timer count range is expressed in ticks. The default value is 12 for 120ms. This value allows a response to include messages that would be sent within the next 120ms range if each tick is 10ms.
NX_PHYSICAL_TRAILER|NX_PHYSICAL_TRAILER|Core||0|255|Specifies the size in bytes of the physical packet trailer and is typically used to reserve storage for things like Ethernet CRCs, etc. The default value is 4 and is defined in nx_api.h.
NX_SECURE_MEMMOVE|NX_SECURE_MEMMOVE|TLS CORE||||This option defines the memory move function.
NX_SECURE_DTLS_COOKIE_LENGTH|NX_SECURE_DTLS_COOKIE_LENGTH|DTLS CORE||1|65535|This option defines the length of DTLS cookie.
NX_PPP_THREAD_TIME_SLICE|NX_PPP_THREAD_TIME_SLICE|PPP||0|2147483647|Time-slice option for PPP threads. By default, this value is TX_NO_TIME_SLICE. This define can be set by the application prior to inclusion of nx_ppp.h.By default, it is TX_NO_TIME_SLICE.
NX_SECURE_DTLS_RETRANSMIT_TIMEOUT|NX_SECURE_DTLS_RETRANSMIT_TIMEOUT|DTLS CORE||0|2147483647|This option defines the initial DTLS retransmit rate.
NXD_MQTT_SOCKET_TIMEOUT|NXD_MQTT_SOCKET_TIMEOUT|MQTT Client||0x0|0xFFFFFFFF|Defines the time out in the TCP socket disconnect call when disconnecting from the MQTT server in timer ticks. The default value is NX_WAIT_FOREVER.
NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_PREDICTION_RESISTANCE|NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_PREDICTION_RESISTANCE|CRYPTO DRBG||0|65535|This option defines drbg prediction resistance.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TIMEOUT_SEND|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TIMEOUT_SEND|WEB Server||0|2147483647|Specifies the number of ThreadX ticks that internal services will suspend for in internal nx_tcp_socket_send() calls. The default value is set to 10 seconds (10 * NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NX_DHCPV6_PACKET_TIME_OUT|NX_DHCPV6_PACKET_TIME_OUT|DHCP||0|2147483647|Time out in seconds for allocating a packet from the Client packet pool. The default value is 3 seconds.
NX_DISABLE_UDP_INFO|NX_DISABLE_UDP_INFO|UDP||||Defined, disables UDP information gathering.
NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_NO_ADDRS_AVAILABLE|NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_NO_ADDRS_AVAILABLE|DHCP||||This defines the status option message for : NX_DHCPV6_STATUS_MESSAGE_NO_ADDRS_AVAILABLE. The default value is "IA OPTION NOT GRANTED-NO ADDRESSES AVAILABLE".
NX_DHCPV6_PACKET_POOL_SIZE|NX_DHCPV6_PACKET_POOL_SIZE|DHCP||0|65535|Defines the Server packet pool size for packets the Server will allocate to send DHCPv6 messages out. The default value is (10 * NX_DHCPV6_PACKET_SIZE).
NX_DNS_CLIENT_USER_CREATE_PACKET_POOL|NX_DNS_CLIENT_USER_CREATE_PACKET_POOL|DNS||||This enables the DNS Client to let the application create and set the DNS Client packet pool. By default this option is disabled, and the DNS Client creates its own packet pool in nx_dns_create.
NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_ROUTER_ADVERTISEMENT_PROCESS|NX_DISABLE_ICMPV6_ROUTER_ADVERTISEMENT_PROCESS|ICMP||||Defined, disables NetX Duo from processing information received in IPv6 router advertisement packets.
NX_CRYPTO_CBC_MAX_BLOCK_SIZE|NX_CRYPTO_CBC_MAX_BLOCK_SIZE|CRYPTO CORE||1|65535|This option defines cbc max block size. The default value is 16.
NX_DHCP_CLIENT_OPTIONS_MAX|NX_DHCP_CLIENT_OPTIONS_MAX|DHCP||1|65535|This is size of the array in the DHCP Client instance for holding the all the requested options in the parameter request list in the current session. The default value is 12.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_SESSION_MAX|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_SESSION_MAX|WEB Server||0|65535|Specifies the number of simultaneous sessions for an HTTP or HTTPS Server. A TCP socket and a TLS session (if HTTPS is enabled) are allocated for each session. The default value is set to 2.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MIN_NTP_VERSION|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_MIN_NTP_VERSION|SNTP||0|255|Oldest SNTP version the Client will be able to work with. The NetX Duo SNTP Client default is Version 3.
NX_ENABLE_SOURCE_ADDRESS_CHECK|NX_ENABLE_SOURCE_ADDRESS_CHECK|Core||||Defined, enables the source address of incoming packet to be checked. By default this option is disabled.
NX_SECURE_DTLS_MAXIMUM_RETRANSMIT_TIMEOUT|NX_SECURE_DTLS_MAXIMUM_RETRANSMIT_TIMEOUT|DTLS CORE||0|2147483647|This option defines the maximum DTLS retransmit rate. The default value is 60 * NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE.
NX_DHCPV6_NUM_TIME_SERVERS|NX_DHCPV6_NUM_TIME_SERVERS|DHCP||1|65535|Number of time servers to store to the client record. The default value is 1.
NX_DHCPV6_DEFAULT_T2_TIME|NX_DHCPV6_DEFAULT_T2_TIME|DHCP||0|65535|The time in seconds assigned by the Server on a Client address lease for when the Client should begin rebinding its IP address assuming its attempt to renew failed. The default value is 3000 seconds.
NX_ENABLE_ICMP_ADDRESS_CHECK|NX_ENABLE_ICMP_ADDRESS_CHECK|ICMP||||Defined, the destination address of ICMP packet is checked. The default is disabled. An ICMP Echo Request destined to an IP broadcast or IP multicast address will be silently discarded.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_THREAD_TIME_SLICE|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_THREAD_TIME_SLICE|SNTP||0|2147483647|This option sets the time slice of the scheduler allows for Client thread execution. The default NetX Duo SNTP Client size is TX_NO_TIME_SLICE.
NX_SECURE_MEMCPY|NX_SECURE_MEMCPY|TLS CORE||||This option defines the memory copy function.
NX_DHCP_ARP_PROBE_NUM|NX_DHCP_ARP_PROBE_NUM|DHCP||0|2147483647|Defines the number of ARP probes sent for determining if the IP address assigned by the DHCP server is already in use. The value is defaulted to 3 probes.
NX_DELAY_FIRST_PROBE_TIME|NX_DELAY_FIRST_PROBE_TIME|Core||0|65535|Specifies the delay in seconds before the first solicitation is sent out for a cache entry in the STALE state. Defined in nx_nd_cache.h, the default value is 5.
NX_IPV6_NEIGHBOR_CACHE_SIZE|NX_IPV6_NEIGHBOR_CACHE_SIZE|IP||1|65535|Specifies the number of entries in the IPv6 Neighbor Cache table. Defined in nx_nd_cache.h, the default value is 16.
NX_MDNS_RR_TTL_HOST|NX_MDNS_RR_TTL_HOST|mDNS||0|65535|TTL value for resource records with host name, in second. The default value is 120 for 120s.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_THREAD_TIME_SLICE|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_THREAD_TIME_SLICE|WEB Server||0|2147483647|The number of timer ticks the Server thread is allowed to run before yielding to threads of the same priority. The default value is 2.
NX_DISABLE_ASSERT|NX_DISABLE_ASSERT|Core||||Defined, disables ASSERT checks in the source code. By default this option is not defined.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_THREAD_PRIORITY|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_THREAD_PRIORITY|SNTP||0|255|This option sets the Client thread priority. The NetX Duo SNTP Client default value is 2.
NX_DISABLE_LOOPBACK_INTERFACE|NX_DISABLE_LOOPBACK_INTERFACE|IP||||Defined, disables NetX Duo support for the loopback interface.
NX_CRYPTO_ECDSA_SCRATCH_BUFFER_SIZE|NX_CRYPTO_ECDSA_SCRATCH_BUFFER_SIZE|CRYPTO ECDSA||1|65535|This option defines crypto ecdsa scratch buffer size.
NX_IP_ROUTING_TABLE_SIZE|NX_IP_ROUTING_TABLE_SIZE|IP||1|65535|Defined, sets the maximum number of entries in the IPv4 static routing table, which is a list of an outgoing interface and the next hop addresses for a given destination address. The default value is 8 and is defined in nx_api.h. This symbol is used only if NX_ENABLE_IP_STATIC_ROUTING is defined.
NX_PPP_DNS_OPTION_DISABLE|NX_PPP_DNS_OPTION_DISABLE|PPP||||If defined, the primary DNS Server Option is disabled in the IPCP response. By default this option is not defined.
NX_NAT_ENABLE|NX_NAT_ENABLE|Core||||Defined, NetX Duo is built with NAT process. By default this option is not defined. This option can be defined only when NX_DISABLE_IPV4 is not selected.
NX_WEB_HTTP_NO_FILEX|NX_WEB_HTTP_NO_FILEX|WEB Server||||Creates a stub file for FileX API. For systems working without FileX When a FileSystem is needed this option should be set to flase FileX should be enabled.
NX_MAX_MULTICAST_GROUPS|NX_MAX_MULTICAST_GROUPS|IGMP||0|65535|Specifies the maximum number of multicast groups that can be joined. The default value is 7 and is defined in nx_api.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_ND_MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH|NX_ND_MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH|Core||0|65535|Symbol that defines the maximum number of packets queued up for Neighbor Discovery cache to be resolved. By default this symbol is set to 4.
NX_ENABLE_VLAN|NX_ENABLE_VLAN|Core||||Defined, the VLAN feature is enabled. Note: Require driver support to use APIs from this file. A quick check in driver is to search for NX_LINK_RAW_PACKET_SEND. VLAN APIs are not supported if not found.
NX_IPV6_PREFIX_LIST_TABLE_SIZE|NX_IPV6_PREFIX_LIST_TABLE_SIZE|IP||1|65535|Specifies the size of the prefix table. Prefix information is obtained from router advertisements and is part of the IPv6 address configuration. Defined in nx_api.h, the default value is 8.
NX_SECURE_TLS_DISABLE_PROTOCOL_VERSION_DOWNGRADE|NX_SECURE_TLS_DISABLE_PROTOCOL_VERSION_DOWNGRADE|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables protocol version downgrade for TLS client.
NX_DHCP_SUBNET_MASK|NX_DHCP_SUBNET_MASK|DHCP||0x00000000|0xFFFFFF00|This is the subnet mask the DHCP Client should be configured with. The default value is set to 0xFFFFFF00.
NX_DNS_QUEUE_DEPTH|NX_DNS_QUEUE_DEPTH|DNS||0|65535|Sets the maximum number of packets to store on the socket receive queue. The default value is 5.
NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TIMEOUT_ACCEPT|NX_WEB_HTTP_SERVER_TIMEOUT_ACCEPT|WEB Server||0|2147483647|Specifies the number of ThreadX ticks that internal services will suspend for in internal nx_tcp_server_socket_accept() calls. The default value is set to (1 * NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NXD_MQTT_SECURE_MEMCPY|NXD_MQTT_SECURE_MEMCPY|MQTT Client||||Define memcpy function used internal.
NX_PPP_DEBUG_LOG_ENABLE|NX_PPP_DEBUG_LOG_ENABLE|PPP||||If defined, internal PPP debug log is enabled.
NX_AUTO_IP_ANNOUNCE_INTERVAL|NX_AUTO_IP_ANNOUNCE_INTERVAL|AUTO_IP||0|65535|The number of seconds to wait between sending announces. By default, this value is defined as 2.
NX_DISABLE_IPV6_DAD|NX_DISABLE_IPV6_DAD|IP||||Defined, this option disables Duplicate Address Detection (DAD) during IPv6 address assignment. Addresses are set either by manual configuration or through Stateless Address Auto Configuration.
NX_DNS_PACKET_ALLOCATE_TIMEOUT|NX_DNS_PACKET_ALLOCATE_TIMEOUT|DNS||0|2147483647|This sets the timeout option for allocating a packet from the DNS client packet pool. The default value is 1 second (1*NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NX_SNTP_UPDATE_TIMEOUT_INTERVAL|NX_SNTP_UPDATE_TIMEOUT_INTERVAL|SNTP||0|65535|The interval (seconds) at which the SNTP Client timer updates the SNTP Client time remaining since the last valid update received, and the unicast Client updates the poll interval time remaining before sending the next SNTP update request. The default value is 1.
NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE|NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE|IP||0|65535|Defined, specifies the number of ThreadX timer ticks in one second. The default value is derived from the ThreadX symbol TX_TIMER_TICKS_PER_SECOND, which by default is set to 100 (10ms timer). Applications shall exercise caution when modifying this value, as the rest of the NetX Duo modules derive timing information from NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE.
NX_SECURE_DTLS_MAXIMUM_RETRANSMIT_RETRIES|NX_SECURE_DTLS_MAXIMUM_RETRANSMIT_RETRIES|DTLS CORE||0|65535|This option defines the maximum retransmit retries for DTLS handshake packet.
NX_DEBUG_PACKET|NX_DEBUG_PACKET|Core||||Defined, enables the optional debug packet dumping available in the RAM Ethernet network driver.
NX_TCP_MAXIMUM_RETRIES|NX_TCP_MAXIMUM_RETRIES|TCP||0|65535|Specifies how many data transmit retries are allowed before the connection is deemed broken. The default value is 10, which represents 10 retries, and is defined in nx_tcp.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_DNS_TYPE_OF_SERVICE|NX_DNS_TYPE_OF_SERVICE|DNS||||Type of service required for the DNS UDP requests. By default, this value is defined as NX_IP_NORMAL for normal IP packet service.
NX_MAX_MULTICAST_SOLICIT|NX_MAX_MULTICAST_SOLICIT|Core||0|65535|Specifies the number of Neighbor Solicitation messages NetX Duo transmits as part of the IPv6 Neighbor Discovery protocol when mapping between IPv6 address and MAC address is required. Defined in nx_nd_cache.h, the default value is 3.
NX_WEB_HTTP_MAX_PASSWORD|NX_WEB_HTTP_MAX_PASSWORD|WEB Server||0|65535|Specifies the number of bytes allowed in a client supplied password. The default value is set to 20.
NX_DHCP_MAX_RETRANS_TIMEOUT|NX_DHCP_MAX_RETRANS_TIMEOUT|DHCP||0|2147483647|Specifies the maximum wait option for receiving a DHCP Server reply to client message before retransmitting the message. The default value is 64 seconds.
NX_DHCPV6_MUTEX_WAIT|NX_DHCPV6_MUTEX_WAIT|DHCP||0x0|0xFFFFFFFF|Time out option for obtaining an exclusive lock on a DHCPv6 Client mutex. The default value is TX_WAIT_FOREVER.
NX_DNS_ENABLE_EXTENDED_RR_TYPES|NX_DNS_ENABLE_EXTENDED_RR_TYPES|DNS||||This enables the DNS Client to query on additional DNS record types in (e.g. CNAME, NS, MX, SOA, SRV and TXT).
NX_SECURE_RNG_CHECK_COUNT|NX_SECURE_RNG_CHECK_COUNT|TLS CORE||1|65535|This option defines the random number check for duplication.
NX_DHCP_PACKET_POOL_SIZE|NX_DHCP_PACKET_POOL_SIZE|DHCP||1|65535|Specifies the size of the DHCP Client packet pool. The default value is (5 *NX_DHCP_PACKET_PAYLOAD) which will provide four packets plus room for internal packet pool overhead.
NX_DISABLE_ICMP_TX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_ICMP_TX_CHECKSUM|ICMP||||Defined, disables both ICMPv4 and ICMPv6 checksum computation on transmitted ICMP packets. This option is useful where the network interface driver is able to compute the ICMPv4 and ICMPv6 checksum, and the application does not use the IP fragmentation feature or IPsec feature. By default this option is not defined.
NX_TCP_MSS_MINIMUM|NX_TCP_MSS_MINIMUM|TCP||0|65535|Symbol that defines the minimal MSS value NetX Duo TCP module accepts. This feature is enabled by NX_ENABLE_TCP_MSS_CHECK.
NX_TCP_MAX_OUT_OF_ORDER_PACKETS|NX_TCP_MAX_OUT_OF_ORDER_PACKETS|TCP||0|65535|Symbol that defines the maximum number of out-of-order TCP packets can be kept in the TCP socket receive queue. This symbol can be used to limit the number of packets queued in the TCP receive socket, preventing the packet pool from being starved. By default this symbol is not defined, thus there is no limit on the number of out of order packets being queued in the TCP socket.
NX_MDNS_PROBING_RETRANSMIT_COUNT|NX_MDNS_PROBING_RETRANSMIT_COUNT|mDNS||0|65535|The number of retransmitted probing messages. The default value is 3.
NX_AUTO_IP_DEBUG|NX_AUTO_IP_DEBUG|AUTO_IP||||This option enables printing a debugging trace using printf.
NX_PPP_BASE_TIMEOUT|NX_PPP_BASE_TIMEOUT|PPP||0|2147483647|This defines the period rate (in timer ticks) that the PPP thread task is woken to check for PPP events. The default value is 1*NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE (100 ticks).
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_INVALID_UPDATE_LIMIT|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_INVALID_UPDATE_LIMIT|SNTP||0|65535|The limit on the number of consecutive invalid updates received from the Client server in either broadcast or unicast mode. When this limit is reached, the Client sets the current SNTP Server status to invalid (NX_FALSE) although it will continue to try to receive updates from the Server. The NetX Duo SNTP Client default is 3.
NX_MDNS_DISABLE_SERVER|NX_MDNS_DISABLE_SERVER|mDNS||||Disables the mDNS/DNS-SD server functionality. Without the server functionality, the mDNS/DNS-SD module does not announce services provided by local host, nor does it respond to mDNS enquiries. This symbol is not defined by default. <b>NX_MDNS_DISABLE_SERVER and NX_MDNS_DISABLE_CLIENT cannot be enabled simultaneously.
NX_AUTO_IP_PROBE_MIN|NX_AUTO_IP_PROBE_MIN|AUTO_IP||0|65535|The minimum number of seconds to wait between sending probes. By default, this value is defined as 1.
NX_PHYSICAL_HEADER|NX_PHYSICAL_HEADER|Core||0|255|Specifies the size in bytes of the physical header of the frame. The default value is 16 (based on a typical 14-byte Ethernet frame aligned to 32-bit boundary) and is defined in nx_api.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included, such as in nx_user.h.
NX_DISABLE_ICMPV4_TX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_ICMPV4_TX_CHECKSUM|ICMP||||Defined, disables ICMPv4 checksum computation on transmitted ICMP packets. This option is defined automatically if NX_DISABLE_ICMP_TX_CHECKSUM is defined. By default this option is not defined.
NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_UNIQUE_DELAY|NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_UNIQUE_DELAY|mDNS||0|2147483647|The delay, in ticks, in responding to a query to a service that is unique to the local network. The default value is 1 tick for 10ms.
NX_ENABLE_DUAL_PACKET_POOL|NX_ENABLE_DUAL_PACKET_POOL|Core||||Defined, allows the stack to use two packet pools, one with large payload size and one with smaller payload size. By default this option is not enabled.
NX_ENABLE_EXTENDED_NOTIFY_SUPPORT|NX_ENABLE_EXTENDED_NOTIFY_SUPPORT|Core||||Defined, enables more callback hooks in the stack. These callback functions are used by the BSD wrapper layer. By default this option is not defined.
NetXDuo_Version|NetXDuo version|Version||||NetXDuo version
NetXDuo_Generate_Init_Code|NetXDuo Generate Init Code|NetXDuo Core Init||||Default value true, Generate NetXDuo Core Init.
NetXDuo_Application_Thread_Name|NetXDuo Application Thread Name|NetXDuo Core Init||||Default value "app_nx_thread_entry" for NetXDuo Application Thread Name.
NX_APP_THREAD_STACK_SIZE|NetXDuo Application Thread Stack Size|NetXDuo Core Init||1024|102400|Default value for NetXDuo Application Thread Stack Size is 1024
NX_APP_THREAD_PRIORITY|NetXDuo Application Thread Priority|NetXDuo Core Init||10|1024|Default value 10 for NetXDuo Application Thread Priority.
NX_APP_PACKET_POOL_SIZE|NetXDuo Pool Size in number of Packets|NetXDuo Core Init||5|255|Default value for the NetXDuo Packet Pool Size in number of packets is 5.
NX_APP_IP_INSTANCE_THREAD_SIZE|NetXDuo IP Instance Thread Size|NetXDuo Core Init||1024|102400|Default value for the IP Instance Thread Size is 1024.
Initialize_ICMP_protocol|Initialize ICMP protocol|NetXDuo Protocols||||By Default ICMP protocol is enabled.
Initialize_TCP_protocol|Initialize TCP protocol|NetXDuo Protocols||||By Default TCP protocol is enabled.
Initialize_DHCP_protocol|Initialize DHCP protocol|NetXDuo Protocols||||By Default DHCP protocol is enabled. When enabled UDP protocol is enabled automatically and couldn't be disabled.
Initialize_UDP_protocol|Initialize UDP protocol|NetXDuo Protocols||||UDP protocol is enabled automatically and couldn't be disabled, when DHCP protocol is enabled.
NetXDuo_Static_IP_address|NetXDuo Ethernet IP Address|NetXDuo Protocols||||Should follow this format : X.X.X.X E.g., 192.168.1.1 or 255.255.255.0
NetXDuo_Application_NetMask|NetXDuo Ethernet NetMask Address|NetXDuo Protocols||||Should follow this format : X.X.X.X E.g., 192.168.1.1 or 255.255.255.0
NX_SECURE_TLS_MINIMUM_CERTIFICATE_SIZE|NX_SECURE_TLS_MINIMUM_CERTIFICATE_SIZE|TLS CORE||0|65535|This option defines a minimum reasonable size for a TLS X509 certificate. This is used in checking for * errors in allocating certificate space. The size is determined by assuming a 512-bit RSA key, MD5 hash, and a rough estimate of other data. It is theoretically possible for a real certificate to be smaller, but in that case, bypass the error checking by re-defining this macro. Approximately: 64(RSA) + 16(MD5) + 176(ASN.1 + text data, common name, etc)
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_NTP_VERSION|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_NTP_VERSION|SNTP||0|255|SNTP version used by the Client The NetX Duo SNTP Client API was based on Version 4. The default value is 3.
NX_REACHABLE_TIME|NX_REACHABLE_TIME|Core||0|65535|Specifies the time out in seconds for a cache entry to exist in the REACHABLE state with no packets received from the cache destination IPv6 address. Defined in nx_nd_cache.h, the default value is 30.
NXD_MQTT_REQUIRE_TLS|NXD_MQTT_REQUIRE_TLS|MQTT Client||||Defined, application must use TLS to connect to MQTT broker. This feature requires NX_SECURE_ENABLE defined. By default, this symbol is not defined.
NX_PPP_DISABLE_CHAP|NX_PPP_DISABLE_CHAP|PPP||||If defined, internal PPP CHAP logic is removed, including the MD5 digest logic.
NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_DUID_VENDOR_ASSIGNED_ID|NX_DHCPV6_SERVER_DUID_VENDOR_ASSIGNED_ID|DHCP||||Create a Server DUID with a vendor assigned ID. Note the DUID type must be set NX_DHCPV6_DUID_TYPE_VENDOR_ASSIGNED.
NX_PPP_NAME_SIZE|NX_PPP_NAME_SIZE|PPP||0|65535|Specifies the size of “name” strings used in authentication. The default value is set to 32bytes, but can be redefined prior to inclusion of *nx_ppp.h.
NX_ENABLE_LOW_WATERMARK|NX_ENABLE_LOW_WATERMARK|IP||||Defined, enables NetX Duo packet pool low watermark feature. Application sets low watermark value. On receiving TCP packets, if the packet pool low watermark is reached, NetX Duo silently discards the packet by releasing it, preventing the packet pool from starvation. By default this feature is not enabled.
NX_MDNS_RR_DELETE_DELAY_TIMER_COUNT|NX_MDNS_RR_DELETE_DELAY_TIMER_COUNT|mDNS||0|2147483647|The delay for deleting a resource record when the TTL of this record is zero, in ticks, The default value is 100 ticks for 1 second (NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NX_SECURE_ENABLE_ECJPAKE_CIPHERSUITE|NX_SECURE_ENABLE_ECJPAKE_CIPHERSUITE|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables ECJPAKE ciphersuites for DTLS.
NX_FRAGMENT_IMMEDIATE_ASSEMBLY|NX_FRAGMENT_IMMEDIATE_ASSEMBLY|IP||||Defined, allows IPv4 and IPv6 reassembly logic to execute right away after receiving an IP fragment. By default this option is not defined.
NX_ENABLE_IP_ID_RANDOMIZATION|NX_ENABLE_IP_ID_RANDOMIZATION|IP||||Defined, this option enables random IP id. By default, IP id is increased by one for each packet.
NX_AUTO_IP_RATE_LIMIT_INTERVAL|NX_AUTO_IP_RATE_LIMIT_INTERVAL|AUTO_IP||0|65535|The number of seconds to extend the wait period when the total number of conflicts is exceeded. By default, this value is defined as 60.
NX_SECURE_ENABLE_AEAD_CIPHER|NX_SECURE_ENABLE_AEAD_CIPHER|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables AEAD ciphersuites.
NX_SECURE_TLS_SNI_EXTENSION_DISABLED|NX_SECURE_TLS_SNI_EXTENSION_DISABLED|TLS CORE||||This option disables Server Name Indication (SNI) extension.
NX_SECURE_TLS_MASTER_SIZE|NX_SECURE_TLS_MASTER_SIZE|TLS CORE||1|65534|Defines the size of master secret.
NX_SECURE_TLS_KEY_MATERIAL_SIZE|NX_SECURE_TLS_KEY_MATERIAL_SIZE|TLS CORE||1|65534|Defines the size of key material.
NX_SECURE_CUSTOM_SECRET_GENERATION|NX_SECURE_CUSTOM_SECRET_GENERATION|TLS CORE||||Enables the user to pass pointers of customized secret generation functions to TLS.
NX_DISABLE_TCP_INFO|NX_DISABLE_TCP_INFO|TCP||||Defined, disables TCP information gathering.
NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_MUTEX_PUT|NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_MUTEX_PUT|CRYPTO DRBG||||Defined, this option enables drbg mutex put.
NX_DISABLE_RX_SIZE_CHECKING|NX_DISABLE_RX_SIZE_CHECKING|IP||||Defined, disables the size checking on received packets.
NX_SECURE_MEMSET|NX_SECURE_MEMSET|TLS CORE||||This option defines the memory set function.
NX_DHCP_TYPE_OF_SERVICE|NX_DHCP_TYPE_OF_SERVICE|DHCP||||Type of service required for the DHCP UDP requests. By default, this value is defined as NX_IP_NORMAL to indicate normal IP packet service.
NX_DISABLE_ICMPV4_RX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_ICMPV4_RX_CHECKSUM|ICMP||||Defined, disables ICMPv4 checksum computation on received ICMP packets. This option is defined automatically if NX_DISABLE_ICMP_RX_CHECKSUM is defined. By default this option is not defined.
NX_MDNS_QUERY_MAX_TIMER_COUNT|NX_MDNS_QUERY_MAX_TIMER_COUNT|mDNS||0|2147483647|The maximum time interval, in ticks, between two queries. The default value is 360000 for 60 seconds.
NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_BLOCK_LENGTH|NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_BLOCK_LENGTH|CRYPTO DRBG||1|65535|This option defines the drbg block length. The default value is NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_BLOCK_LENGTH_AES.
NX_DISABLE_IGMP_INFO|NX_DISABLE_IGMP_INFO|IGMP||||Defined, disables IGMP information gathering.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_RTT_REQUIRED|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_RTT_REQUIRED|SNTP||||This option if enabled requires that the SNTP Client calculate round trip time of SNTP messages when applying Server updates to the local clock. The default value is NX_FALSE (disabled).
NX_DHCP_SERVER_HOSTNAME_MAX|NX_DHCP_SERVER_HOSTNAME_MAX|DHCP||1|255|This is size of the buffer for holding the Server host name. The default value is 32.
NX_MDNS_IPV6_ADDRESS_COUNT|NX_MDNS_IPV6_ADDRESS_COUNT|mDNS||0|65535|Maximum IPv6 addresses count of host. The default value is 2.
NX_SECURE_TLS_ENABLE_SSL_3_0|NX_SECURE_TLS_ENABLE_SSL_3_0|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables SSL 3.0 .
NX_DISABLE_IP_INFO|NX_DISABLE_IP_INFO|IP||||Defined, disables IP information gathering.
NX_MAX_LISTEN_REQUESTS|NX_MAX_LISTEN_REQUESTS|TCP||1|65535|Specifies the maximum number of server listen requests. The default value is 10 and is defined in nx_api.h. The application can override the default by defining the value before nx_api.h is included.
NX_ARP_MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH|NX_ARP_MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH|ARP/RARP||0|65535|Specifies the maximum number of packets that can be queued while waiting for an ARP response. The default value is 4 and is defined in nx_api.h.
NX_AUTO_IP_PROBE_WAIT|NX_AUTO_IP_PROBE_WAIT|AUTO_IP||0|65535|The number of seconds to wait before sending first probe. By default, this value is defined as 1.
NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_SEED_BUFFER_LEN|NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_SEED_BUFFER_LEN|CRYPTO DRBG||1|65535|This option defines the drbg seed buffer length. The default value is 256.
NX_SECURE_ENABLE_PSK_CIPHERSUITES|NX_SECURE_ENABLE_PSK_CIPHERSUITES|TLS CORE||||Defined, this option enables Pre-Shared Key (PSK) functionality. It does not disable digital certificates.
NX_DHCP_THREAD_PRIORITY|NX_DHCP_THREAD_PRIORITY|DHCP||0|255|Priority of the DHCP thread. By default, this value specifies that the DHCP thread runs at priority 3.
NX_DHCP_CLIENT_SEND_ARP_PROBE|NX_DHCP_CLIENT_SEND_ARP_PROBE|DHCP||||Defined, this enables the DHCP Client to send an ARP probe after IP address assignment to verify the assigned DHCP address is not owned by another host. By default, this option is disabled.
NX_PPP_MAX_PAP_PROTOCOL_RETRIES|NX_PPP_MAX_PAP_PROTOCOL_RETRIES|PPP||0|65535|This defines the max number of retries if the PPP times out before sending another PAP authentication request message. When this number is reached the PPP handshake is aborted and the link status is down. The default value is 20.
NX_MDNS_POOF_MIN_COUNT|NX_MDNS_POOF_MIN_COUNT|mDNS||0|65535|The number of queries that no multicast response, then the host may take this as an indication that the record may no longer be valid. The default value is 2.
NX_SECURE_TLS_USE_SCSV_CIPHPERSUITE|NX_SECURE_TLS_USE_SCSV_CIPHPERSUITE|TLS CORE||||This option enables SCSV ciphersuite in ClientHello message.
NX_DHCPV6_TIME_TO_LIVE|NX_DHCPV6_TIME_TO_LIVE|DHCP||0|65535|The number of times a Client packet is forwarded by a network router before the packet is discarded. The default value is 0x80.
NX_MDNS_UDP_TYPE_OF_SERVICE|NX_MDNS_UDP_TYPE_OF_SERVICE|mDNS||||Define UDP socket create options.
NX_AUTO_IP_ANNOUNCE_WAIT|NX_AUTO_IP_ANNOUNCE_WAIT|AUTO_IP||0|65535|The number of seconds to wait before sending announcement. By default, this value is defined as 2.
NX_PACKET_ALIGNMENT|NX_PACKET_ALIGNMENT|Core||0|65535|Defined, specifies the alignment requirement, in bytes, for starting address of the packet payload area. This option deprecates NX_PACKET_HEADER_PAD and NX_PACKET_HEADER_PAD_SIZE. By default this option is defined to be 4, making the starting address of the payload area 4-byte aligned.
NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_INTERVAL|NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_INTERVAL|mDNS||0|2147483647|The time interval, in ticks, in responding to a query to ensure an interval of at least 1s since the last time the record was multicast. The default value is 100 ticks (NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NX_DNS_CLIENT_CLEAR_QUEUE|NX_DNS_CLIENT_CLEAR_QUEUE|DNS||||This enables the DNS Client to clear old DNS messages off the receive queue before sending a new query. Removing these packets from previous DNS queries prevents the DNS Client socket queue from overflowing and dropping valid packets.
NX_DHCP_RESTART_WAIT|NX_DHCP_RESTART_WAIT|DHCP||0|2147483647|Defines the length of time the DHCP Client waits to restart DHCP if the IP address assigned to the DHCP Client is already in use. The value is defaulted to 10 seconds.
NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_TC_DELAY_MIN|NX_MDNS_RESPONSE_TC_DELAY_MIN|mDNS||0|2147483647|The minimum delay, in ticks, in responding to a query with TC bit. The default value is 40 ticks for 400ms.
NX_IP_STATUS_CHECK_WAIT_TIME|NX_IP_STATUS_CHECK_WAIT_TIME|IP||0|65535|Define the amount of time to sleep in nx_ip_(interface_)status_check
NX_DHCP_TIME_INTERVAL|NX_DHCP_TIME_INTERVAL|DHCP||0|2147483647|Interval in seconds when the DHCP Client timer expiration function executes. This function updates all the timeouts in the DHCP process e.g. if messages should be retransmitted or DHCP Client state changed. By default, this value is 1 second.
NX_SNTP_CLIENT_RANDOMIZE_ON_STARTUP|NX_SNTP_CLIENT_RANDOMIZE_ON_STARTUP|SNTP||||This determines if the SNTP Client in unicast mode should send its first SNTP request with the current SNTP server after a random wait interval. It is used in cases where significant numbers of SNTP Clients are starting up simultaneously to limit traffic congestion on the SNTP Server. The default value is NX_FALSE.
NX_IPV6_STATELESS_AUTOCONFIG_CONTROL|NX_IPV6_STATELESS_AUTOCONFIG_CONTROL|IP||||Defined, allows NetX Duo to disable stateless address autoconfiguration feature. By default this option is not enabled.
NX_IPV6_DESTINATION_TABLE_SIZE|NX_IPV6_DESTINATION_TABLE_SIZE|IP||1|65535|Specifies the number of entries in the IPv6 destination table. This stores information about next hop addresses for IPv6 addresses. Defined in nx_api.h, the default value is 8.
NX_ENABLE_TCP_QUEUE_DEPTH_UPDATE_NOTIFY|NX_ENABLE_TCP_QUEUE_DEPTH_UPDATE_NOTIFY|TCP||||Defined, allows the application to install a callback function that is invoked when the TCP transmit queue depth is no longer at maximum value. This callback serves as an indication that the TCP socket is ready to transmit more data. By default this option is not enabled.
NXD_MQTT_KEEPALIVE_TIMER_RATE|NXD_MQTT_KEEPALIVE_TIMER_RATE|MQTT Client||0|2147483647|Defines the MQTT timer rate, in ThreadX timer ticks. This timer is used to keep track of the time since last MQTT control message was sent, and sends out an MQTT PINGREQ message before the keep-alive time expires. This timer is activated if the client connects to the broker with a keep-alive timer value set. The default value is TX_TIMER_TICKS_PER_SECOND, which is a one-second timer. The default value is TX_TIMER_TICKS_PER_SECOND.
NX_DNS_MAX_RETRANS_TIMEOUT|NX_DNS_MAX_RETRANS_TIMEOUT|DNS||0|2147483647|The maximum retransmission timeout on a DNS query to a specific DNS server. The default value is 64 seconds (64 * NX_IP_PERIODIC_RATE).
NX_DISABLE_ICMP_RX_CHECKSUM|NX_DISABLE_ICMP_RX_CHECKSUM|ICMP||||Defined, disables both ICMPv4 and ICMPv6 checksum computation on received ICMP packets. This option is useful when the network interface driver is able to verify the ICMPv4 and ICMPv6 checksum, and the application does not use the IP fragmentation feature or the IPsec feature. By default this option is not defined.
NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_MUTEX_GET|NX_CRYPTO_DRBG_MUTEX_GET|CRYPTO DRBG||||Defined, this option enables drbg mutex get.
NX_SECURE_TLS_MINIMUM_MESSAGE_BUFFER_SIZE|NX_SECURE_TLS_MINIMUM_MESSAGE_BUFFER_SIZE|TLS CORE||0|65535|This option defines the minimum size for the TLS message buffer. It is determined by a number of factors, but primarily the expected size of the TLS handshake Certificate message (sent by the TLS server) that may contain multiple certificates of 1-2KB each. The upper limit is determined by the length field in the TLS header (16 bit), and is 64KB.
NX_PPP_VALUE_SIZE|NX_PPP_VALUE_SIZE|PPP||0|65535|Specifies the size of “value” strings used in CHAP authentication. The default value is set to 32bytes, but can be redefined prior to inclusion of nx_ppp.h.
TX_TIMER_TICKS_PER_SECOND|TX_TIMER_TICKS_PER_SECOND|Core||||Define the common timer tick reference for use by other middleware components
NX_APP_MEM_POOL_SIZE|NetXDuo memory pool size|Memory Configuration||512|262144|Default memory pool size for the NETXDUOX application. <font color="red">The allocated memory for all enabled middelwares should not exceed the total size of available memory.</font>
AZRTOS_APP_MEM_ALLOCATION_METHOD|Memory Allocation|Core||||
NX_CLOUD_ENABLED|NX_CLOUD_ENABLED|MQTT Client||||
FILEX_ENABLED|FILEX_ENABLED|Core||||
LAN_8742|LAN_Phy_Interface|BSP||0|1|
ETH_ON|ETH Interface Enabled|Eth||0|1|
NX_ENABLE_TCPIP_OFFLOAD|NX_ENABLE_TCPIP_OFFLOAD|Core||||Offload TCP/IP processing to the underlining HW
NX_DHCP_SERVER_THREAD_STACK_SIZE|NX_DHCP_SERVER_THREAD_STACK_SIZE|DHCP||1024|2048|Define the DHCP server thread stack size.
NX_DHCP_SERVER_NAME|NX_DHCP_SERVER_NAME|DHCP||||Define name of DHCP server.
NX_MDNS_DISABLE_CLIENT|NX_MDNS_DISABLE_CLIENT|mDNS||||Disable the mDNS Client functionality. By default, mDNS client function is enabled. <b>NX_MDNS_DISABLE_CLIENT and NX_MDNS_DISABLE_SERVER cannot be enabled simultaneously.
NX_CRYPTO_AES_USE_RAM_TABLES|NX_CRYPTO_AES_USE_RAM_TABLES|CRYPTO CORE||||When defined the AES Tabled are moved to RAM.
NX_SECURE_TLS_REQUIRE_RENEGOTIATION_EXT|NX_SECURE_TLS_REQUIRE_RENEGOTIATION_EXT|TLS CORE||||Defines whether or not the connection should be terminated immediately upon failure to receive the secure renegotiation extension during the initial handshake. By default, the connection is not terminated.
NX_SECURE_TLS_DISABLE_CLIENT_INITIATED_RENEGOTIATION|NX_SECURE_TLS_DISABLE_CLIENT_INITIATED_RENEGOTIATION|TLS CORE||||Disables client-initiated renegotiation for TLS servers. In some instances, client-initiated renegotiation can become a possible denial-of-service vulnerability.
NX_SECURE_TLS_DISABLE_SECURE_RENEGOTIATION|NX_SECURE_TLS_DISABLE_SECURE_RENEGOTIATION|TLS CORE||||Disable secure session renegotiation extension.
NX_PPP_OPTION_MESSAGE_LENGTH|NX_PPP_OPTION_MESSAGE_LENGTH|PPP||64|128|Size of the NAK list.
NETXDUO_MEM_POOL_VAR_NAME|NetXDuo MemPool Name|Memory Configuration||||Default NetXDuo memory pool var name <font color="red"> <b>This is a variable name. It should be C compliant declaration, Otherwise compilation errors will be generated in the project. </b> </font>

[Values]
# параметр|значение|подпись
